{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/dev/nightly.clj | sed -n '1,300p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns nightly\n     2\t  \"The nightly suite driver — ONE script for every host.\n     3\t\n     4\t   The lane assignment is an argument, not a different script: shiva and\n     5\t   jupiter run the same file from the same commit, so a fix to the harness\n     6\t   never has to be copied between hosts. (Before 2026-11-01 each host had its\n     7\t   own hand-written ~/ci/nightly-*.sh; they drifted — jupiter's bypassed mise\n     8\t   entirely and pinned its PATH to `latest` symlinks, so babashka and flutter\n     9\t   resolved to different versions on the two hosts.)\n    10\t\n    11\t   Usage:\n    12\t     bb src/dev/nightly.clj <clone-dir> <lanes> [parallel] [--now]\n    13\t                               [--pin-publish | --pin-read]\n    14\t\n    15\t     lanes       comma-separated subset of: jvm,node,dart\n    16\t     parallel    per-lane parallelism (default: 12)\n    17\t     --now       ignore the 03:00/17:00 Vietnam windows (cron fires hourly)\n    18\t     --pin-publish   resolve origin/master, publish {run-id, sha, ts} for the\n    19\t                     other host (the pin authority; shiva)\n    20\t     --pin-read      check out the pinned SHA, refusing a pin whose Vietnam\n    21\t                     date is not today (advisory + nonzero exit otherwise)\n    22\t     --pin-peer H    with --pin-read: the host holding the pin (the authority,\n    23\t                     e.g. shiva.stigmergy.systems). Without it the pin is read\n    24\t                     from this host's own file, which only the publisher writes.\n    25\t\n    26\t   Exit: 0 all lanes green; 1 any red, missing, or infrastructure failure.\n    27\t\n    28\t   Toolchain: mise owns it. `mise install` runs first so a pin change in\n    29\t   mise.toml actually reaches the host — the step whose absence let the two\n    30\t   hosts drift (build-n-test.md documents this order).\"\n    31\t  (:require [babashka.fs :as fs]\n    32\t            [babashka.process :as p]\n    33\t            [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    34\t            [clojure.string :as str]))\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\t(def home (System/getProperty \"user.home\"))\n    38\t(def results-dir (str home \"/ci/nightly-results\"))\n    39\t(def pin-file (str home \"/ci/nightly-pin.txt\"))\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t(def child-path\n    43\t  (str home \"/.local/share/mise/shims:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:\"\n    44\t       (System/getenv \"PATH\")))\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t(defn- psh\n    48\t  \"p/shell with the mise shims on the child PATH (never replaces the env).\"\n    49\t  [opts & cmd]\n    50\t  (apply p/shell (update opts :extra-env #(merge {\"PATH\" child-path} %)) cmd))\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t(defn- run-cmd!\n    54\t  \"Run cmd to a fresh log with stdout/stderr merged; return the exit code.\"\n    55\t  [dir out-file cmd]\n    56\t  (:exit (apply psh {:dir dir\n    57\t                     :out (io/file out-file)\n    58\t                     :err :out\n    59\t                     :continue true}\n    60\t                cmd)))\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\t(defn- vn-date\n    64\t  []\n    65\t  (str/trim (:out (psh {:out :string :extra-env {\"TZ\" \"Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\"}}\n    66\t                       \"date\" \"+%Y%m%d\"))))\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\t(defn- vn-hour\n    70\t  []\n    71\t  (str/trim (:out (psh {:out :string :extra-env {\"TZ\" \"Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\"}}\n    72\t                       \"date\" \"+%H\"))))\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t(defn- git-out\n    76\t  [dir & args]\n    77\t  (str/trim (:out (apply psh {:dir dir :out :string :err :string :continue true} \"git\" args))))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(defn- slow-namespaces\n    81\t  \"The ^:slow test namespaces, derived from the tree (never a static list).\"\n    82\t  [clone]\n    83\t  (->> (apply psh {:dir clone :out :string :continue true}\n    84\t              [\"grep\" \"-rl\" \"\\\\^:slow\" \"test\" \"--include=*.clj\" \"--include=*.cljc\"])\n    85\t       :out\n    86\t       str/split-lines\n    87\t       (remove str/blank?)\n    88\t       (map (fn [path]\n    89\t              (-> path\n    90\t                  (str/replace #\"^test/\" \"\")\n    91\t                  (str/replace #\"\\.clj[cd]?$\" \"\")\n    92\t                  (str/replace \"/\" \".\")\n    93\t                  (str/replace \"_\" \"-\"))))\n    94\t       sort))\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\t(defn- run-pool\n    98\t  \"Run f over items with at most n in flight; return {item exit}.\"\n    99\t  [n f items]\n   100\t  (let [queue (atom (vec items))\n   101\t        take-one (fn []\n   102\t                   (locking queue\n   103\t                     (let [c @queue]\n   104\t                       (when (seq c)\n   105\t                         (reset! queue (subvec c 1))\n   106\t                         (first c)))))\n   107\t        results (atom {})]\n   108\t    (->> (range (min n (count items)))\n   109\t         (mapv (fn [i]\n   110\t                 (future\n   111\t                   (loop []\n   112\t                     (if-let [x (take-one)]\n   113\t                       (do (swap! results assoc x (f x)) (recur))\n   114\t                       i)))))\n   115\t         (mapv deref))\n   116\t    @results))\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\t(defn- lane-jvm\n   120\t  [clone par out summary]\n   121\t  (let [quick (run-cmd! clone (str out \"/jvm-quick.log\")\n   122\t                        [\"bb\" \"test:quick-sharded\" \"--workers\" (str par)])\n   123\t        slow-nss (slow-namespaces clone)\n   124\t        slow (run-pool par\n   125\t                       (fn [nss]\n   126\t                         (run-cmd! clone (str out \"/slow-\" nss \".log\")\n   127\t                                   [\"clojure\" \"-M:test\" \"-i\" :slow \"-n\" nss]))\n   128\t                       slow-nss)\n   129\t        slow-red (count (remove zero? (vals slow)))]\n   130\t    (spit summary (str \"jvm-quick rc=\" quick \" (sharded, \" par \" workers)\\n\"\n   131\t                       \"jvm-slow namespaces=\" (count slow-nss)\n   132\t                       \" red=\" slow-red \"\\n\")\n   133\t          :append true)\n   134\t    (when-not (zero? quick) (throw (ex-info \"jvm quick tier red\" {:rc quick})))\n   135\t    (when (pos? slow-red) (throw (ex-info \"jvm slow tier red\" {:red slow-red})))))\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\t(defn- lane-node\n   139\t  [clone par out summary]\n   140\t  (let [rc (run-cmd! clone (str out \"/node-shard.log\")\n   141\t                     [\"bb\" \"src/dev/node_shard.clj\" clone (str par)])]\n   142\t    (spit summary (str \"node-shard rc=\" rc \"\\n\") :append true)\n   143\t    (when-not (zero? rc) (throw (ex-info \"node sharded lane red\" {:rc rc})))))\n   144\t\n   145\t\n   146\t(defn- lane-dart\n   147\t  [clone par out summary]\n   148\t  (let [rc (run-cmd! clone (str out \"/dart-shard.log\")\n   149\t                     [\"bb\" \"src/dev/dart_shard.clj\" clone (str par)])]\n   150\t    (spit summary (str \"dart-shard rc=\" rc \"\\n\") :append true)\n   151\t    (when-not (zero? rc) (throw (ex-info \"dart sharded lane red\" {:rc rc})))))\n   152\t\n   153\t\n   154\t(defn -main\n   155\t  [& args]\n   156\t  ;; NB: never pad args with (repeat nil) — destructuring `& rest` off an\n   157\t  ;; infinite lazy seq makes (remove nil? rest) loop forever (2026-11-01).\n   158\t  (let [positional (take-while #(not (str/starts-with? % \"--\")) args)\n   159\t        flag-args (drop (count positional) args)\n   160\t        flags (set (filter #(str/starts-with? % \"--\") flag-args))\n   161\t        pin-peer (some (fn [[a b]] (when (= a \"--pin-peer\") b))\n   162\t                       (partition 2 1 flag-args))\n   163\t        [clone lanes par] positional\n   164\t        clone (or clone (str home \"/ci/datomworld\"))\n   165\t        lanes (set (str/split (or lanes \"jvm,node,dart\") #\",\"))\n   166\t        par (or (some->> par parse-long) 12)\n   167\t        now? (or (contains? flags \"--now\") (= \"1\" (System/getenv \"NOW\")))\n   168\t        publish? (contains? flags \"--pin-publish\")\n   169\t        read-pin? (contains? flags \"--pin-read\")\n   170\t        stamp (.format (java.time.format.DateTimeFormatter/ofPattern \"yyyyMMdd-HHmm\")\n   171\t                       (java.time.LocalDateTime/now))\n   172\t        out (str results-dir \"/\" stamp)\n   173\t        summary (str out \"/summary.txt\")\n   174\t        rc (atom 0)\n   175\t        log (fn [s] (println s) (spit summary (str s \"\\n\") :append true))]\n   176\t    ;; Owner ruling 2026-11-01: the full suite runs exactly twice a day,\n   177\t    ;; 03:00 and 17:00 Vietnam time — 03:00 catches the day's work before the\n   178\t    ;; owner stops coding, 17:00 gives a result they can act on before sleep.\n   179\t    ;; Everything else (the pre-merge gate) runs the affected tests only.\n   180\t    (when-not (or now? (contains? #{\"03\" \"17\"} (vn-hour)))\n   181\t      (println \"outside the 03:00/17:00 Vietnam windows; pass --now to force\")\n   182\t      (System/exit 0))\n   183\t    (fs/create-dirs out)\n   184\t    (when-not (= 0 (:exit (psh {:dir clone :continue true} \"mise\" \"trust\")))\n   185\t      (println \"mise trust failed\"))\n   186\t    (let [ti (run-cmd! clone (str out \"/mise-install.log\") [\"mise\" \"install\"])]\n   187\t      (log (str \"mise-install rc=\" ti))\n   188\t      (when-not (zero? ti) (log \"FAIL: toolchain install\")))\n   189\t    ;; pin protocol\n   190\t    (when-not (zero? (:exit (psh {:dir clone :continue true} \"git\" \"fetch\" \"origin\")))\n   191\t      (log \"FAIL: git fetch\"))\n   192\t    (let [sha (git-out clone \"rev-parse\" \"origin/master\")]\n   193\t      (cond\n   194\t        publish?\n   195\t        (let [line (str \"run-id=\" (vn-date) \"-\" (subs stamp 9 13) \" sha=\" sha \" ts=\"\n   196\t                        (str/trim (:out (psh {:out :string} \"date\" \"-u\" \"+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\"))))]\n   197\t          (spit (str pin-file \".tmp\") line)\n   198\t          (fs/move (str pin-file \".tmp\") pin-file {:replace-existing true})\n   199\t          (log (str \"pin published: \" line))\n   200\t          (psh {:dir clone :continue true} \"git\" \"checkout\" \"-q\" \"--detach\" sha))\n   201\t        read-pin?\n   202\t        (let [line (if pin-peer\n   203\t                     (str/trim (:out (psh {:out :string :continue true}\n   204\t                                          \"ssh\" \"-o\" \"BatchMode=yes\"\n   205\t                                          \"-o\" \"ConnectTimeout=8\"\n   206\t                                          pin-peer \"cat\" pin-file)))\n   207\t                     (when (fs/exists? pin-file) (str/trim (slurp pin-file))))\n   208\t              prid (some->> line (re-find #\"run-id=(\\S+)\") second)\n   209\t              psha (some->> line (re-find #\"sha=([0-9a-f]{7,40})\") second)]\n   210\t          (if (and psha (= (subs prid 0 8) (vn-date))\n   211\t                   (zero? (:exit (psh {:dir clone :continue true} \"git\" \"cat-file\" \"-e\" psha))))\n   212\t            (do (psh {:dir clone :continue true} \"git\" \"checkout\" \"-q\" \"--detach\" psha)\n   213\t                (log (str \"pin read: \" psha \" (run-id \" prid \")\")))\n   214\t            (do (reset! rc 1)\n   215\t                (log (str \"FAIL: pin absent/stale/unverifiable (\" (or prid \"none\") \") — advisory run at \" sha))\n   216\t                (psh {:dir clone :continue true} \"git\" \"checkout\" \"-q\" \"--detach\" sha))))\n   217\t        :else (psh {:dir clone :continue true} \"git\" \"checkout\" \"-q\" \"--detach\" sha)))\n   218\t    (log (str \"nightly \" stamp \" at \" (git-out clone \"log\" \"--oneline\" \"-1\")\n   219\t              \" lanes=\" (str/join \",\" (sort lanes)) \" par=\" par))\n   220\t    (doseq [lane [\"jvm\" \"node\" \"dart\"]]\n   221\t      (when (contains? lanes lane)\n   222\t        (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)]\n   223\t          (try\n   224\t            ((case lane\n   225\t               \"jvm\" lane-jvm\n   226\t               \"node\" lane-node\n   227\t               \"dart\" lane-dart)\n   228\t             clone par out summary)\n   229\t            (log (str lane \" rc=0 secs=\"\n   230\t                      (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0) 1000)))\n   231\t            (catch Exception e\n   232\t              (reset! rc 1)\n   233\t              (log (str \"FAIL \" lane \": \" (ex-message e)\n   234\t                        \" secs=\" (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0) 1000))))))))\n   235\t    (log (str \"done rc=\" @rc))\n   236\t    (System/exit @rc)))\n   237\t\n   238\t\n   239\t(when (= *file* (System/getProperty \"babashka.file\"))\n   240\t  (apply -main *command-line-args*))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,100p' orchestrator-logs/1793511339-remote-test-harness.md && sed -n '35,115p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && sed -n '245,275p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && sed -n '320,375p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,100p' orchestrator-logs/1793511339-remote-test-harness.md && sed -n '35,115p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && sed -n '245,275p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && sed -n '320,375p' docs/agents/build-n-test.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Orchestrator log — remote test harness track (shiva/jupiter)\n\n## 2026-11-01 12:35:39 +07 — subsystem-sharded nightly harness for shiva/jupiter\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-01 05:35:39 GMT\nCoding-Agent: interactive\nSession-ID: sess_b6001731-427a-4431-b74f-97f348558fc2\nTree: master@120ff322 (clean tracked tree apart from two other seats' uncommitted\n  orchestrator-logs edits and codex's in-flight edit to src/dev/dart_shard.clj)\n\nDone: The nightly testing harness was rebuilt so each lane runs sharded by\nsubsystem and concurrently, and so both hosts run identical versioned code.\nLanded on master: `e3704fd9` one nightly driver (`src/dev/nightly.clj`, lanes as an\nargument, mise install first, pin publish/read), `4a28d183` shard output capture to\nFiles (unflushed Writers were silently losing every log under one buffer),\n`120ff322` dao.stream diagnostics (every unclean corpus read collapsed to a bare\nnil), plus earlier `a731d99e`/`e2` fixes to the Node selector and pool, `2bd42461`\ncljd_agg flags, and `mise.toml` pins for babashka and flutter (`5e5b7c7f`).\n`src/dev/node_shard.clj` (work-stealing pool, PAR 12, bundle-inventory validation),\n`src/dev/dart_shard.clj` (one full cljd compile, per-subsystem shard dirs, ONE\nflutter invocation), and `src/dev/nightly.clj` are the three drivers; both hosts\nrun the same blobs from the same commit.\n\nDecisions:\n- Lane split kept as the owner ratified: jupiter JVM, shiva Node, Dart on either.\n- Work-stealing over waves: `partition-all` idled 4 of 6 slots when fast shards\n  finished (load 3.59); the pool raised it to 10.8.\n- `babashka`/`flutter` were `\"latest\"` in mise.toml, which resolves per host at\n  install time (1.12.218 vs 1.13.225; 3.47.1 vs 3.47.8) — pinned, and the wrappers\n  now run `mise install` (the step whose absence caused the drift).\n- Two host-local bash wrappers were replaced by the one versioned driver; they\n  still exist on disk because live runs were launched by them.\n- DEVIATION, recorded honestly: harness fixes were committed under the owner's\n  running instruction to make the harness work (\"fix it\", \"yes\", \"delegate the fix\n  to codex\") rather than at each commit. From this entry forward, step 9 gating\n  applies: no staging or committing without explicit instruction.\n\nVerification:\n- Jupiter JVM lane, complete: quick sharded 14/14 green 1,023 s; slow tier 52\n  namespaces 5,645 s with 7 reds (all yang.python.* + yin.vm.semantic.derive-test).\n- Shiva Node lane at 120ff322, in flight: 10/14 shards done, 0 failures, incl.\n  dao.stream rc=0 129 s; the 4 heavy shards (yang.python, yin.repl, yin.vm,\n  uncovered) still running.\n- Output capture proven by experiment (131 KB captured across stdout+stderr,\n  survives non-zero exit, truncates per run).\n- Not verified: no complete tri-host run; the Dart lane has never executed on\n  either host (jupiter failed at cljd compile, shiva never got there); the two\n  XML-free measurements of Node/Dart wall time therefore do not exist yet.\n\nDelegates: codex gpt-6.1-sol — nightly-plan review (REVISE: R1/R3/R4/R6),\n  node-shard diagnosis (found the `--test` two-arg bug that made every \"shard\" run\n  the full suite), node-shard fix (capture + apply bug in nightly.clj), and the\n  in-flight dart-shard diagnosis on jupiter. kimi k3.1-pro — independent second\n  opinion on the node-shard memory question (independently found `:cache-root` is\n  not settable through build-level --config-merge).\n\nNext:\n1. Accept/verify codex's dart-shard diagnosis (in flight on jupiter), then the\n   first real Dart-lane measurement.\n2. Finish the shiva Node lane; record the wall time and whether yang.python/yin.vm\n   complete or stall (their cost is real computation in dao.space.query/unify per\n   the profile, not GC).\n3. Run the same suite on the other host with the same driver to settle the\n   Node/Dart routing question by measurement.\n4. Independent review (different family from codex) of the harness diffs before\n   relying on them for gate decisions.\n5. Owner decision pending: re-enable the 03:00 VN cron entries (currently\n   cancelled); pin or leave `android-sdk = \"latest\"` in mise.toml.\n#\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` runs twice daily on the remote hosts (03:00/17:00 VN);\n# a MERGE needs only the affected tests (bb test:changed) -- owner ruling 2026-11-01.\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\n# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\n# overlap lanes, see \"Remote test servers\" below).\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\nbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\nbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\n                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\n                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\n                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\n```\n\n### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\n\n`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\nreach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\nmerge-base with master, plus fixtures that mention a changed resource path,\ntests that walk a changed tree, and each src file's `_test` by convention.\nA walker is a file calling file-seq, fs/glob, fs/list-dir,\nfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\nio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\n(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\nlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\nneeded builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\n`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\ntypo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\nland a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\nchange (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\nantlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\nas for a change to the core everything requires (yin.vm engine,\ndao.stream, codecs) and before a big merge. Not seen: dynamic loads\n(`requiring-resolve`, `resolve`), paths or walk roots built at run time,\nand spawned programs that changed (target/yin-repl.js, Dart peers).\n\n### Sharded quick JVM feedback and change routing\n\n```sh\nbb test:quick-sharded                           # Full G3-sized JVM quick lane, 4 workers\nbb test:quick-sharded --changed src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\nbb test:quick-sharded --base master --workers 6  # Changed selection, explicit worker limit\nbb test:quick-sharded --list --changed src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\nbb test:routed docs/agents/build-n-test.md       # Explicit changed paths (absolute OK)\nbb test:routed --dry-run deps.edn               # Print dispatch; executes no gate\nbb test:routed                                 # Git change set, same base as test:changed\nbb deps:npm                                    # Content-checked local npm ci\nbb -cp src/dev -m quick-sharded-test            # Runner/routing/cache self-tests\n```\n\n`test:quick-sharded` is a JVM-only execution alternative for broad G2 and\nthe JVM portion of G3. Without selection flags it selects every JVM test;\n`--changed FILE...` or `--base REF` uses `affected/select` and\n`affected/lane-tests`, exactly as `test:changed:clj` does. Wide input selects\nthe full JVM set here. It never changes `test:changed`'s selection or exit-2\nsemantics. `--workers N` must be positive (default 4 on the laptop).\n- **Layer 1 (Space & UI)**: `dao.space`, `dao.gui`, `dao.postgraphics`\n- **Layer 2 (Execution Engine)**: `yin.vm.ucf`, `yin.vm`\n- **Layer 3 (Languages & Interop)**: `yin.repl`, `yang.python`, `yang.base`\n- **Layer 4 (Applications & Demos)**: `demo`, `world`\n- **Infrastructure**: `dev`, `bench`\n\nPrerequisites (`build:yin-repl-peer`, `build:yin-repl-node`, `gen:antlr`)\nand lane serialization (`[:clj :cljd]`) are derived purely from text reach of the\nselected namespaces and run automatically when needed.\n\n#### Gate Ladder (docs/design/test.subsystems.md)\n\n1. **G0 Iterate**: Run only the subsystem's JVM lane (`bb test:sub:clj <own>` or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`).\n2. **G1 Checkpoint**: Run the three-lane subsystem test (`bb test:sub <own>`). Proves the home suite across all three hosts before reporting ready.\n3. **G2 Land**: Run `bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes (plus `bb test:sub <own> --slow` if slow tests are present). Covers dependents across the change (for foundation subsystems like `dao.stream` or `dao.jing`, this correctly runs nearly the full suite).\n4. **G3 Master (merged in place by the 2026-11-01 owner ruling)**: The landing gate\n   for a change is the **tests that cover the feature being built** — `bb test:changed`\n   (G2) already includes the reverse-require closure of the changed files, and a wide\n   change still routes to the full quick lane. The complete suite is no longer a\n   per-merge gate: it runs twice a day on the remote hosts (see \"Cadence\" below), so a\n   break is caught within hours without charging every merge ~400 minutes of slow tier.\n5. **G4 Release**: Full or slow test run before a big release or cross-cutting merge\n   (`bb test:slow` or `bb test:all`), at each phase boundary of a multi-phase track\n   (owner decision 2026-10-12), and implicitly twice daily by the scheduled run below.\n   G0 to G3 run the quick tier; G4 runs the slow tier.\n\n\nThe linker-over-DHT end-to-end gate (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md,\nslice L5) is two tests:\n\n- `yin.repl.dht-process-test` (JVM lane only): real `yin.repl.main`\naggregated lanes only run namespaces that still exist under `test/`, but a\nstale file can silently pass a plain `cljd test`. Run `rm -rf test/cljd-out`\nbefore relying on that to prove a deletion or rename took effect.\n\n## Test tiers: quick and slow\n\nThe suite has two tiers so that slow tests run less often than quick ones\n(owner decision, 2026-10-12).\n\n- **Quick tier:** every test not tagged `^:slow`. `bb test:clj` or\n  `clojure -M:test -e :slow` on the JVM; the Node and Dart lanes skip the\n  guarded bodies (`dao.test-slow/guard`) unless `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1`.\n- **Slow tier:** the tagged deftests. `bb test:slow` or\n  `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>` on the JVM.\n- **The tagging rule** is the one above (\"When to tag a test slow\"): a deftest that\n  takes about 5 s or more run alone. On 2026-10-12 every JVM test namespace and every\n  deftest in the 22 slowest namespaces were timed on a 48-core Linux server, and the\n  **63 deftests at 5 s or more** were tagged: `^:slow` on the deftest, plus the guard\n  wrapper in `.cljc` files. 37 are guarded, 26 are `^:slow` only (`.clj` files and\n  `:clj` reader-conditional branches). Those 22 namespaces now hold **168 slow tests**\n  in all (some were already tagged). Per-test times are not in the repo: measure again\n  with the method below before changing the cut.\n- **Cadence (owner ruling 2026-11-01):** a merge needs only the tests that cover the\n  feature being built — the affected/dependent set from `bb test:changed` (or\n  `bb test:sub <own> --slow` when the change touches slow-tagged code). The FULL suite,\n  including the slow tier, runs **twice a day: 03:00 and 17:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh** on the\n  remote hosts (`src/dev/nightly.clj`; 03:00 catches the day's work before the owner\n  stops coding, 17:00 gives a result they can act on before sleeping). The measured long\n  set is ~400 minutes of serial slow-tier work, so it cannot be a per-merge cost; a\n  break is instead caught by the next scheduled run, at most ~12 hours later.\n  The schedule is expressed as an hourly cron plus a Vietnam-time guard inside the\n  driver, so it is immune to the DST shifts of either host's local timezone.\n\nMeasured (2026-10-12, origin master plus the tags, Linux servers; see \"Remote test\nservers\" for how to run them):\n\n| Run | Time |\n|---|---|\n| Full JVM lane, one process, before tagging (shiva) | 70 min |\n| Full JVM lane, sharded by subsystem, before tagging (jupiter, 13 shards, 8 at a time) | 46.5 min, set by `yin.repl.python-antlr-test` |\n| **Quick tier, sharded by subsystem (jupiter, same 13 shards)** | **5 min 3 s**, 4055 tests, all shards exit 0; longest shards `yang.python` 253 s and `yin.vm.ucf` 204 s |\n| **Slow tier (shiva, one JVM per namespace, 6 at a time)** | **53 min**, 22 namespaces, 168 tests, all exit 0; longest `yin.repl.python-antlr-test` 3183 s (about 1580 s alone on the laptop) |\n\nThe quick tier has exactly 63 fewer tests than the untagged suite (4118 to 4055).\nSome quick parts are still 25 to 69 s when a namespace is run alone (`e2e-c2`,\n`prelude-parity`, `int-ops`, `holder.driver`, `compose-rows`): many tests each just\nunder the 5 s cut (the Python e2e per-test floor is about 2 to 3 s), not shared setup.\nA lower cut would shrink the quick tier further and move more tests to the slow tier.\n\n**How the per-test times were measured.** To time every deftest of a namespace alone,\nrun it without the test runner's alias main (the `:test` alias's `-m cognitect.test-runner`\notherwise swallows `-e`, and every JVM runs the whole suite):\n\n```sh\nNS=<namespace> clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:t {:extra-paths [\"test\"]}}}' -M:t timing.clj\n# timing.clj: require the namespace, for each deftest var that is not ^:slow:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
