{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/dev/affected.clj | sed -n '1,290p' && nl -ba src/dev/node_shard.clj | sed -n '1,300p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns affected\n     2\t  \"The test namespaces a change can affect, and a runner for them.\n     3\t\n     4\t   The changed files are `git diff --name-only <base>` plus the staged and\n     5\t   untracked files; base defaults to `git merge-base HEAD master`. Each\n     6\t   .clj .cljc .cljs .cljd file under src/ and test/ (not test/cljd-out) is\n     7\t   read for its first ns form, once per host feature (:clj :cljs :cljd),\n     8\t   so every reader-conditional branch counts. The affected tests are the\n     9\t   test namespaces (under test/, named *-test or holding a deftest) in the\n    10\t   reverse transitive closure of the changed namespaces, plus:\n    11\t   - a changed src file's conventional test (src/cljc/a/b.cljc selects\n    12\t     test/a/b_test.*), required or not;\n    13\t   - for a non-code file (a fixture under test/resources, a src resource),\n    14\t     the closure of every namespace whose text mentions its path or\n    15\t     basename: fixtures are read by path, not required;\n    16\t   - for any changed file, the closure of every namespace that walks its\n    17\t     tree with (file-seq (io/file \\\"<root>\\\")).\n    18\t   Ignored: docs/ collab/ build/ target/ node_modules/ cljd-out and *.md\n    19\t   (but a .md under test/resources is a fixture). Wide: deps.edn bb.edn\n    20\t   shadow-cljs.edn tests.edn package*.json pubspec.* .clj-kondo/ antlr/\n    21\t   src/dev/; a wide change selects every test and runs nothing.\n    22\t\n    23\t   Run with babashka:\n    24\t     bb src/dev/affected.clj [--list] [--base REF] [--lane clj|cljs|cljd]\n    25\t                             [--changed FILE...]\n    26\t   --list prints the selection and each changed file's reason; no run.\n    27\t   --lane restricts to one lane (repeatable; default all three).\n    28\t   --changed replaces the git query with the given files.\n    29\t   Without --list the selected lanes run in parallel, each logging to\n    30\t   target/profile/changed-<lane>.log, and a summary table follows.\n    31\t   Exit: 0 pass (or nothing selected), 1 a lane failed or bad input,\n    32\t   2 wide change: run bb test.\"\n    33\t  (:require\n    34\t    [babashka.fs :as fs]\n    35\t    [babashka.process :as p]\n    36\t    [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    37\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n    38\t    [edamame.core :as e]))\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(def code-exts #{\"clj\" \"cljc\" \"cljs\" \"cljd\"})\n    42\t(def lanes [:clj :cljs :cljd])\n    43\t(def log-dir \"target/profile\")\n    44\t(def wide-exit 2)\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t(def ignored-prefixes\n    48\t  [\"docs/\" \"collab/\" \"build/\" \"target/\" \"node_modules/\" \"test/cljd-out/\"\n    49\t   \"lib/cljd-out/\"])\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(def wide-files\n    53\t  #{\"deps.edn\" \"bb.edn\" \"shadow-cljs.edn\" \"tests.edn\" \"package.json\"\n    54\t    \"package-lock.json\" \"pubspec.yaml\" \"pubspec.lock\" \"mise.toml\"\n    55\t    \".cljstyle\"})\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(def wide-prefixes [\".clj-kondo/\" \"antlr/\" \"src/dev/\"])\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(defn- starts-with-any?\n    62\t  [path prefixes]\n    63\t  (some #(str/starts-with? path %) prefixes))\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\t(defn classify\n    67\t  \"One of :ignored :wide :code :resource for the repo-relative `path`.\"\n    68\t  [path]\n    69\t  (cond (starts-with-any? path ignored-prefixes) :ignored\n    70\t        (str/starts-with? path \"test/resources/\") :resource\n    71\t        (str/ends-with? path \".md\") :ignored\n    72\t        (or (wide-files path) (starts-with-any? path wide-prefixes)) :wide\n    73\t        (and (starts-with-any? path [\"src/\" \"test/\"])\n    74\t             (code-exts (fs/extension path))) :code\n    75\t        :else :resource))\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    79\t;; ns forms\n    80\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    81\t\n    82\t(def ^:private dep-clauses #{:require :use :require-macros :use-macros})\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\t(defn ns-name-of\n    86\t  [form]\n    87\t  (second form))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn- libspec-deps\n    91\t  \"Namespaces named by one libspec: a symbol, [lib & opts] or a prefix\n    92\t   list [prefix suffix [suffix & opts] ...]. Strings (npm) name none.\"\n    93\t  [spec]\n    94\t  (cond (symbol? spec) [spec]\n    95\t        (sequential? spec)\n    96\t        (let [[head & more] spec]\n    97\t          (cond (not (symbol? head)) []\n    98\t                (or (empty? more) (keyword? (first more))) [head]\n    99\t                :else (->> more\n   100\t                           (filter (some-fn symbol? sequential?))\n   101\t                           (mapcat libspec-deps)\n   102\t                           (map #(symbol (str head \".\" %))))))\n   103\t        :else []))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(defn form-deps\n   107\t  \"Namespaces an ns form loads through :require :use :require-macros\n   108\t   and :use-macros.\"\n   109\t  [form]\n   110\t  (->> (rest form)\n   111\t       (filter seq?)\n   112\t       (filter (comp dep-clauses first))\n   113\t       (mapcat rest)\n   114\t       (mapcat libspec-deps)\n   115\t       set))\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(defn- read-opts\n   119\t  [feature]\n   120\t  {:all true\n   121\t   :read-cond :allow\n   122\t   :features #{feature}\n   123\t   :auto-resolve (fn [k] (if (= :current k) 'user k))\n   124\t   :readers (fn [_tag] identity)\n   125\t   :eof ::eof})\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\t(defn- first-ns-form\n   129\t  [text feature]\n   130\t  (let [rdr (e/reader text)\n   131\t        opts (e/normalize-opts (read-opts feature))]\n   132\t    (loop []\n   133\t      (let [form (e/parse-next rdr opts)]\n   134\t        (cond (= ::eof form) nil\n   135\t              (and (seq? form) (= 'ns (first form))) form\n   136\t              :else (recur))))))\n   137\t\n   138\t\n   139\t(defn ns-info\n   140\t  \"{:ns name :deps #{...}} of the first ns form of `text`, the deps the\n   141\t   union over the :clj :cljs and :cljd readings and a reading no branch\n   142\t   but :default matches.\"\n   143\t  [text]\n   144\t  (let [forms (if (str/includes? text \"#?\")\n   145\t                (keep #(first-ns-form text %) (conj lanes ::none))\n   146\t                (keep identity [(first-ns-form text :clj)]))]\n   147\t    {:ns (some ns-name-of forms)\n   148\t     :deps (into #{} (mapcat form-deps) forms)}))\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\t(def ^:private code-path\n   152\t  #\"^(?:src/(?:clj|cljc|cljs|cljd|dev)/|test/)(.+)\\.(?:clj|cljc|cljs|cljd)$\")\n   153\t\n   154\t\n   155\t(defn path->ns\n   156\t  \"The namespace a code path declares by convention (for deleted files).\"\n   157\t  [path]\n   158\t  (when-let [[_ rel] (re-find code-path path)]\n   159\t    (symbol (-> rel (str/replace \"/\" \".\") (str/replace \"_\" \"-\")))))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn convention-test-paths\n   163\t  \"test/a/b_test.<ext> candidates for src/<host>/a/b.<ext>.\"\n   164\t  [path]\n   165\t  (when-let [[_ rel] (re-find #\"^src/[^/]+/(.+)\\.(?:clj|cljc|cljs|cljd)$\"\n   166\t                              path)]\n   167\t    (mapv #(str \"test/\" rel \"_test.\" %) [\"clj\" \"cljc\" \"cljs\" \"cljd\"])))\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t(defn mentions?\n   171\t  \"True when `text` mentions `path` or its basename.\"\n   172\t  [text path]\n   173\t  (or (str/includes? text path)\n   174\t      (str/includes? text (str (fs/file-name path)))))\n   175\t\n   176\t\n   177\t(def ^:private walk-call\n   178\t  #\"file-seq|fs/glob|fs/list-dir|fs/walk-file-tree|\\.listFiles\")\n   179\t\n   180\t\n   181\t(def ^:private path-call\n   182\t  #\"\\((?:io/file|fs/file|fs/path|fs/glob|java\\.io\\.File\\.|File\\.)\\s\")\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(defn- string-end\n   186\t  \"Index of the quote closing the string literal opened at `i`.\"\n   187\t  [^String text i]\n   188\t  (loop [j (inc i)]\n   189\t    (cond (>= j (count text)) j\n   190\t          (= \\\\ (.charAt text j)) (recur (+ j 2))\n   191\t          (= \\\" (.charAt text j)) j\n   192\t          :else (recur (inc j)))))\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\t(defn- literal-args\n   196\t  \"The string literals that are direct arguments of the call whose open\n   197\t   paren is at `start` in `text`. Nested forms, comments and character\n   198\t   literals are skipped.\"\n   199\t  [^String text start]\n   200\t  (loop [i (inc start)\n   201\t         depth 1\n   202\t         acc []]\n   203\t    (if (or (zero? depth) (>= i (count text)))\n   204\t      acc\n   205\t      (let [c (.charAt text i)]\n   206\t        (cond (= \\\" c) (let [end (string-end text i)]\n   207\t                         (recur (inc end) depth\n   208\t                                (cond-> acc\n   209\t                                  (= 1 depth)\n   210\t                                  (conj (subs text (inc i)\n   211\t                                              (min end (count text)))))))\n   212\t              (= \\\\ c) (recur (+ i 2) depth acc)\n   213\t              (= \\; c) (recur (or (some-> (str/index-of text \"\\n\" i) inc)\n   214\t                                  (count text))\n   215\t                              depth acc)\n   216\t              (#{\\( \\[ \\{} c) (recur (inc i) (inc depth) acc)\n   217\t              (#{\\) \\] \\}} c) (recur (inc i) (dec depth) acc)\n   218\t              :else (recur (inc i) depth acc))))))\n   219\t\n   220\t\n   221\t(defn- trim-root\n   222\t  [root]\n   223\t  (let [r (-> root\n   224\t              (str/replace #\"^(?:\\./)+\" \"\")\n   225\t              (str/replace #\"/+$\" \"\"))]\n   226\t    (if (str/blank? r) \".\" r)))\n   227\t\n   228\t\n   229\t(defn scanner-roots\n   230\t  \"The roots a text that walks a directory (file-seq, fs/glob,\n   231\t   fs/list-dir, fs/walk-file-tree, .listFiles) may walk: every string\n   232\t   literal argument of every io/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob,\n   233\t   java.io.File. or File. call in it, so a let-bound root counts. A root\n   234\t   built at run time (str, a computed path) does not.\"\n   235\t  [text]\n   236\t  (if-not (re-find walk-call text)\n   237\t    []\n   238\t    (let [m (re-matcher path-call text)]\n   239\t      (->> (loop [acc []]\n   240\t             (if (.find m)\n   241\t               (recur (into acc (literal-args text (.start m))))\n   242\t               acc))\n   243\t           (map trim-root)\n   244\t           distinct\n   245\t           vec))))\n   246\t\n   247\t\n   248\t(defn under-root?\n   249\t  \"True when `path` is `root` or lies in its tree; \\\".\\\" holds every\n   250\t   path.\"\n   251\t  [root path]\n   252\t  (or (= \".\" root) (= root path) (str/starts-with? path (str root \"/\"))))\n   253\t\n   254\t\n   255\t(defn index-entry\n   256\t  \"What the selection needs to know about one code file.\"\n   257\t  [path text]\n   258\t  (let [{:keys [ns deps]} (ns-info text)]\n   259\t    {:path path\n   260\t     :ext (fs/extension path)\n   261\t     :ns ns\n   262\t     :deps deps\n   263\t     :text text\n   264\t     :roots (scanner-roots text)\n   265\t     :test? (boolean\n   266\t              (and ns\n   267\t                   (str/starts-with? path \"test/\")\n   268\t                   (or (str/ends-with? (name ns) \"-test\")\n   269\t                       (re-find #\"\\((?:[\\w.-]+/)?deftest\\s\" text))))}))\n   270\t\n   271\t\n   272\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   273\t;; Selection\n   274\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   275\t\n   276\t(defn reverse-closure\n   277\t  \"`roots` and every node of `graph` {node #{dep}} that reaches one.\"\n   278\t  [graph roots]\n   279\t  (let [rdeps (reduce-kv (fn [m n deps]\n   280\t                           (reduce #(update %1 %2 (fnil conj #{}) n) m deps))\n   281\t                         {}\n   282\t                         graph)]\n   283\t    (loop [seen (set roots)\n   284\t           todo (vec roots)]\n   285\t      (if-let [n (peek todo)]\n   286\t        (let [new (remove seen (rdeps n))]\n   287\t          (recur (into seen new) (into (pop todo) new)))\n   288\t        seen))))\n   289\t\n   290\t\n     1\t(ns node-shard\n     2\t  \"Node lane sharded by subsystem (the bb mirror of shard-jvm.sh).\n     3\t\n     4\t   One full shadow-cljs compile (:autorun false), then one\n     5\t   `node target/node-tests.js --test=ns1,ns2,...` process per subsystem, up\n     6\t   to PAR at a time. Selection is RUNTIME: shadow's :ns-regexp compile filter\n     7\t   does not remove previously cached test namespaces from the bundle.\n     8\t\n     9\t   Review fixes (gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-10-31) implemented here:\n    10\t   - R1: every requested namespace is validated against the compiled\n    11\t     bundle's own --list inventory before running (the --test selector\n    12\t     silently ignores unknown namespaces).\n    13\t   - R6: per-run immutable out dir (node-shards-$STAMP, -latest symlink);\n    14\t     expected-vs-completed shard check; nonzero exit on red, missing, or\n    15\t     unexplained shards; prerequisite and compile failures are fatal.\n    16\t   - The Dart peer is built (its absence makes peer tests skip).\n    17\t\n    18\t   Usage: bb src/dev/node_shard.clj <clone-dir> [parallel]\n    19\t   Exit: 0 all green; 1 any failure (infra, missing, or red).\"\n    20\t  (:require [babashka.fs :as fs]\n    21\t            [babashka.process :as p]\n    22\t            [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    23\t            [clojure.set :as set]\n    24\t            [clojure.string :as str]))\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\t(def subs\n    28\t  [\"yang.python\" \"yin.repl\" \"yin.vm\" \"yin.vm.ucf\" \"dao.stream\"\n    29\t   \"dao.jing\" \"dao.gui\" \"dao.space\" \"demo\" \"dao.data\"\n    30\t   \"dao.postgraphics\" \"yang.base\" \"dao.base\"])\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t(def ^:private child-path\n    34\t  \"PATH for every child process: mise shims first (npm/node/flutter/bb/clj all\n    35\t   resolve through mise regardless of the caller's ambient PATH), then the\n    36\t   inherited PATH, then the system dirs for env/bash.\"\n    37\t  (str (System/getProperty \"user.home\") \"/.local/share/mise/shims\"\n    38\t       \":/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:\"\n    39\t       (System/getenv \"PATH\")))\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t(defn- psh\n    43\t  \"p/shell with the mise-shims PATH forced into the child environment,\n    44\t   merged over any caller-supplied :env.\"\n    45\t  [opts & cmd]\n    46\t  (apply p/shell (update opts :extra-env #(merge {\"PATH\" child-path} %)) cmd))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn ns->test-ns\n    50\t  \"test/yin/vm/foo_test.cljc -> yin.vm.foo-test (the namespace name).\"\n    51\t  [path]\n    52\t  (-> path\n    53\t      (str/replace #\"^test/\" \"\")\n    54\t      (str/replace #\"\\.clj[cs]$\" \"\")\n    55\t      (str/replace \"/\" \".\")\n    56\t      (str/replace \"_\" \"-\")))\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t(defn cljs-namespaces\n    60\t  \"The cljs test namespaces `bb test:sub:list <s>` reports for subsystem s.\"\n    61\t  [clone s]\n    62\t  (let [{:keys [out]} (psh {:dir clone :out :string :continue true}\n    63\t                           \"bb\" \"test:sub:list\" s)\n    64\t        section (->> (str/split-lines out)\n    65\t                     (drop-while #(not (str/starts-with? % \"cljs:\")))\n    66\t                     (rest)\n    67\t                     (take-while #(re-matches #\"^\\s+\\S.*$\" %))\n    68\t                     (map str/trim)\n    69\t                     (remove str/blank?))]\n    70\t    (vec section)))\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t(defn -main\n    74\t  [& args]\n    75\t  (let [clone (or (first args) (System/getProperty \"user.dir\"))\n    76\t        par   (or (some->> (second args) parse-long) 8)\n    77\t        stamp (.format (java.time.format.DateTimeFormatter/ofPattern \"yyyyMMdd-HHmm\")\n    78\t                       (java.time.LocalDateTime/now))\n    79\t        out   (str clone \"/target-ci/node-shards-\" stamp)\n    80\t        rc    (atom 0)\n    81\t        summary (str out \"/summary.txt\")\n    82\t        fail! (fn [msg]\n    83\t                (reset! rc 1)\n    84\t                (println \"FAIL:\" msg)\n    85\t                (spit summary (str \"FAIL: \" msg \"\\n\") :append true))\n    86\t        log   (fn [msg] (println msg) (spit summary (str msg \"\\n\") :append true))\n    87\t        sh    (fn [out-file cmd]\n    88\t                ;; Each command owns a fresh log. File redirects need no\n    89\t                ;; caller-owned buffer; :err :out avoids two file offsets\n    90\t                ;; overwriting the same path.\n    91\t                (let [{:keys [exit]} (apply psh {:dir clone, :out (io/file out-file), :err :out,\n    92\t                                                 :continue true}\n    93\t                                            cmd)]\n    94\t                  exit))]\n    95\t    (fs/create-dirs out)\n    96\t    (fs/delete-if-exists (str clone \"/target-ci/node-shards-latest\"))\n    97\t    (fs/create-sym-link (str clone \"/target-ci/node-shards-latest\")\n    98\t                        (str \"node-shards-\" stamp))\n    99\t    (log (str \"start \" stamp \" par=\" par))\n   100\t    ;; prerequisites — fatal on failure\n   101\t    ;; npm always through mise exec: mise's npm wrapper execs `node` by bare\n   102\t    ;; name, which fails under any caller PATH that lacks the mise node bin\n   103\t    ;; (mise exec supplies it). The repo's mise.toml pins the node version.\n   104\t    (let [exit (sh (str out \"/npm-ci.log\")\n   105\t                   [\"mise\" \"exec\" \"--\" \"npm\" \"ci\" \"--silent\"])]\n   106\t      (log (str \"npm-ci rc=\" exit))\n   107\t      (when-not (zero? exit) (fail! \"npm ci failed\")))\n   108\t    (doseq [[nm cmd] [[\"build-yin-repl-node\" [\"bb\" \"build:yin-repl-node\"]]\n   109\t                      [\"build-yin-repl-peer\" [\"bb\" \"build:yin-repl-peer\"]]\n   110\t                      [\"gen-antlr\" [\"bb\" \"gen:antlr\"]]]]\n   111\t      (let [exit (sh (str out \"/\" nm \".log\") cmd)]\n   112\t        (log (str nm \" rc=\" exit))\n   113\t        (when-not (zero? exit) (fail! (str nm \" failed\")))))\n   114\t    ;; per-subsystem cljs namespaces; the per-run files are the evidence\n   115\t    (let [lists (into {} (map (fn [s] [s (cljs-namespaces clone s)]) subs))\n   116\t          test-root (str (fs/canonicalize (str clone \"/test\")))\n   117\t          all (->> (file-seq (fs/file test-root))\n   118\t                   (filter #(re-find #\"_test\\.clj[cs]$\" (str %)))\n   119\t                   (map (fn [path]\n   120\t                          (-> (str path)\n   121\t                              (str/replace (str test-root \"/\") \"\")\n   122\t                              ns->test-ns)))\n   123\t                   set)\n   124\t          covered (apply set/union (map set (vals lists)))\n   125\t          uncovered (set/difference all covered)\n   126\t          lists (cond-> lists (seq uncovered)\n   127\t                        (assoc \"uncovered\" (vec uncovered)))]\n   128\t      (log (str \"all=\" (count all) \" covered=\" (count covered)\n   129\t                \" uncovered=\" (count uncovered)))\n   130\t      (doseq [[s nss] lists]\n   131\t        (spit (str out \"/ns-\" s \".txt\") (str/join \"\\n\" nss))))\n   132\t    ;; one full compile, no autorun\n   133\t    (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n   134\t          exit (sh (str out \"/compile.log\")\n   135\t                   [\"clj\" \"-M:cljs\" \"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\"\n   136\t                    \"compile\" \"test\" \"--config-merge\" \"{:autorun false}\"])]\n   137\t      (log (str \"compile-all rc=\" exit\n   138\t                \" secs=\" (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0) 1000)))\n   139\t      (when-not (zero? exit) (fail! \"compile failed\")))\n   140\t    ;; R1: the bundle's own inventory is the authority on what can run\n   141\t    (let [{listing :out} (psh {:dir clone :out :string :continue true}\n   142\t                              \"node\" \"target/node-tests.js\" \"--list\")\n   143\t          bundle (->> (str/split-lines listing)\n   144\t                      (keep #(re-find #\"^Namespace: (\\S+)\" %))\n   145\t                      (map second)\n   146\t                      set)\n   147\t          lists (into {}\n   148\t                      (map (fn [s]\n   149\t                             [s (some->> (str out \"/ns-\" s \".txt\")\n   150\t                                         slurp\n   151\t                                         str/split-lines\n   152\t                                         (remove str/blank?)\n   153\t                                         vec)])\n   154\t                           subs))\n   155\t          lists (cond-> lists\n   156\t                  (.exists (fs/file (str out \"/ns-uncovered.txt\")))\n   157\t                  (assoc \"uncovered\"\n   158\t                         (->> (slurp (str out \"/ns-uncovered.txt\"))\n   159\t                              str/split-lines\n   160\t                              (remove str/blank?)\n   161\t                              vec)))\n   162\t          sel (into {} (map (fn [[s nss]] [s (filterv bundle nss)])) lists)\n   163\t          ;; Absence from the bundle's --list means the lane has no tests in\n   164\t          ;; that namespace (a JVM-only namespace behind a clj reader\n   165\t          ;; conditional compiles to a library with no cljs test vars). That\n   166\t          ;; is a lane exclusion, recorded for the summary — not a failure.\n   167\t          ;; A failure is a namespace the bundle KNOWS that then fails to\n   168\t          ;; run, which the expected-vs-completed check below catches.\n   169\t          exclusions (into {}\n   170\t                           (remove (fn [[_ nss]] (empty? nss)))\n   171\t                           (into {}\n   172\t                                 (map (fn [[s nss]]\n   173\t                                        [s (set/difference (set nss) bundle)]))\n   174\t                                 lists))]\n   175\t      (doseq [[s ex] exclusions]\n   176\t        (log (str \"lane-excluded \" s \": \" (str/join \",\" (sort ex)))))\n   177\t      ;; run up to PAR shards at a time (waves)\n   178\t      (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n   179\t            shards (vec (filter (comp seq sel) (keys sel)))\n   180\t            runs (atom {})\n   181\t            run-one (fn [s]\n   182\t                      (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n   183\t                            {:keys [exit]}\n   184\t                            (psh {:dir clone\n   185\t                                  :out (io/file (str out \"/\" s \".log\"))\n   186\t                                  :err (io/file (str out \"/\" s \".err.log\"))\n   187\t                                  :extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}\n   188\t                                  :continue true}\n   189\t                                 \"node\" \"target/node-tests.js\"\n   190\t                                 ;; ONE argument: shadow 3.3.5's runner accepts\n   191\t                                 ;; only --test=<list>; a separate \"--test\" arg\n   192\t                                 ;; is ignored (\"Unknown arg\") and the worker\n   193\t                                 ;; silently runs the FULL suite (2026-11-01).\n   194\t                                 (str \"--test=\" (str/join \",\" (sel s))))\n   195\t                            secs (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0) 1000)]\n   196\t                        (let [logtxt (try (slurp (str out \"/\" s \".log\"))\n   197\t                                          (catch Exception _ \"\"))\n   198\t                              suspicious (or (str/includes? logtxt \"Unknown arg\")\n   199\t                                             (str/includes? logtxt \"Ran 0 tests\"))]\n   200\t                          (when suspicious\n   201\t                            (fail! (str \"shard \" s \" ran nothing (selection not applied)\")))\n   202\t                          (swap! runs assoc s {:rc exit :secs secs}))\n   203\t                        (spit (str out \"/runs.txt\")\n   204\t                              (str s \" rc=\" exit \" secs=\" secs \"\\n\")\n   205\t                              :append true)))]\n   206\t        ;; WORK-STEALING pool, not waves: a wave scheduler parks the next\n   207\t        ;; shard until every shard in the current batch finishes, so four\n   208\t        ;; 20-second shards leave four slots idle while one heavy shard runs\n   209\t        ;; (observed 2026-11-01: load 3.6 on a 24-thread host). Each worker\n   210\t        ;; pulls the next shard as soon as it finishes, so all PAR slots stay\n   211\t        ;; busy until the queue drains and the wall is the heaviest shard.\n   212\t        (let [queue (atom shards)\n   213\t              take-one (fn []\n   214\t                         (locking queue\n   215\t                           (let [cur @queue]\n   216\t                             (when (seq cur)\n   217\t                               (reset! queue (subvec cur 1))\n   218\t                               (first cur)))))]\n   219\t          (->> (range (min par (count shards)))\n   220\t               (mapv (fn [i]\n   221\t                       (future\n   222\t                         (loop []\n   223\t                           (if-let [s (take-one)]\n   224\t                             (do (run-one s) (recur))\n   225\t                             i)))))\n   226\t               (mapv deref)))\n   227\t        (let [expected (count shards)\n   228\t              done (count @runs)\n   229\t              red (count (filter #(not= 0 (:rc %)) (vals @runs)))\n   230\t              wall (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0) 1000)]\n   231\t          (doseq [[s r] (sort @runs)]\n   232\t            (log (str s \" rc=\" (:rc r) \" secs=\" (:secs r))))\n   233\t          (log (str \"node-sharded lanes=\" done \" red-lanes=\" red\n   234\t                    \" wall=\" wall \"s\"))\n   235\t          (when-not (= expected done)\n   236\t            (fail! (str \"expected \" expected \" shards, completed \" done)))\n   237\t          (when (pos? red)\n   238\t            (fail! (str red \" red shards\"))))))\n   239\t    (log (str \"done rc=\" @rc))\n   240\t    (System/exit @rc)))\n   241\t\n   242\t\n   243\t(when (= *file* (System/getProperty \"babashka.file\"))\n   244\t  (apply -main *command-line-args*))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/dev/dart_shard.clj | sed -n '1,300p' && nl -ba src/dev/quick_sharded.clj | sed -n '1,200p' && cat src/dev/subsystems.edn\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dart-shard\n     2\t  \"Dart lane sharded by subsystem (the bb mirror of shard-jvm.sh).\n     3\t\n     4\t   One full cljd compile (per-namespace incremental in lib/cljd-out; cannot\n     5\t   be parallelized in one clone), then per subsystem a shard directory\n     6\t   emitted by cljd_agg.clj (--only / --shard-dir / --no-compile / --no-run),\n     7\t   and ONE `flutter test` invocation over all emitted directories — Flutter's\n     8\t   test compiler writes a project-wide build/test_cache kernel, so parallel\n     9\t   flutter processes in one clone race (gpt-6.1-sol review R3, 2026-10-31).\n    10\t   Per-subsystem attribution survives via the emitted directory paths in the\n    11\t   output.\n    12\t\n    13\t   Review fixes implemented here (R1, R3, R6): the uncovered residual shard\n    14\t   is emitted and run; emission failures are fatal; per-run immutable out\n    15\t   dir (dart-shards-$STAMP, -latest symlink); prerequisite and compile\n    16\t   failures are fatal; nonzero exit on any failure.\n    17\t\n    18\t   Usage: bb src/dev/dart_shard.clj <clone-dir> [concurrency]\n    19\t   Exit: 0 all green; 1 any failure.\"\n    20\t  (:require [babashka.fs :as fs]\n    21\t            [babashka.process :as p]\n    22\t            [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    23\t            [clojure.set :as set]\n    24\t            [clojure.string :as str]))\n    25\t\n    26\t\n    27\t(def subs\n    28\t  [\"yang.python\" \"yin.repl\" \"yin.vm\" \"yin.vm.ucf\" \"dao.stream\"\n    29\t   \"dao.jing\" \"dao.gui\" \"dao.space\" \"demo\" \"dao.data\"\n    30\t   \"dao.postgraphics\" \"yang.base\" \"dao.base\"])\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t(def ^:private child-path\n    34\t  \"PATH for every child process: mise shims first (npm/node/flutter/bb/clj all\n    35\t   resolve through mise regardless of the caller's ambient PATH), then the\n    36\t   inherited PATH, then the system dirs for env/bash.\"\n    37\t  (str (System/getProperty \"user.home\") \"/.local/share/mise/shims\"\n    38\t       \":/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:\"\n    39\t       (System/getenv \"PATH\")))\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t(defn- psh\n    43\t  \"p/shell with the mise-shims PATH forced into the child environment.\"\n    44\t  [opts & cmd]\n    45\t  (apply p/shell (assoc opts :extra-env {\"PATH\" child-path}) cmd))\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\t(defn cljd-namespaces\n    49\t  \"The cljd test namespaces `bb test:sub:list <s>` reports for subsystem s.\"\n    50\t  [clone s]\n    51\t  (let [{:keys [out]} (psh {:dir clone :out :string :continue true}\n    52\t                           \"bb\" \"test:sub:list\" s)\n    53\t        section (->> (str/split-lines out)\n    54\t                     (drop-while #(not (str/starts-with? % \"cljd:\")))\n    55\t                     (rest)\n    56\t                     (take-while #(re-matches #\"^\\s+\\S.*$\" %))\n    57\t                     (map str/trim)\n    58\t                     (remove str/blank?))]\n    59\t    (vec section)))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(defn -main\n    63\t  [& args]\n    64\t  (let [clone (or (first args) (System/getProperty \"user.dir\"))\n    65\t        conc  (or (some->> (second args) parse-long) 8)\n    66\t        stamp (.format (java.time.format.DateTimeFormatter/ofPattern \"yyyyMMdd-HHmm\")\n    67\t                       (java.time.LocalDateTime/now))\n    68\t        out   (str clone \"/target-ci/dart-shards-\" stamp)\n    69\t        rc    (atom 0)\n    70\t        summary (str out \"/summary.txt\")\n    71\t        fail! (fn [msg]\n    72\t                (reset! rc 1)\n    73\t                (println \"FAIL:\" msg)\n    74\t                (spit summary (str \"FAIL: \" msg \"\\n\") :append true))\n    75\t        log   (fn [msg] (println msg) (spit summary (str msg \"\\n\") :append true))]\n    76\t    (fs/create-dirs out)\n    77\t    (fs/delete-if-exists (str clone \"/target-ci/dart-shards-latest\"))\n    78\t    (fs/create-sym-link (str clone \"/target-ci/dart-shards-latest\")\n    79\t                        (str \"dart-shards-\" stamp))\n    80\t    (log (str \"start \" stamp \" conc=\" conc))\n    81\t    ;; Each command owns a fresh log: File redirects avoid unflushed Writers,\n    82\t    ;; and :err :out merges both streams through one file offset.\n    83\t    ;; the Dart peer; its absence makes peer tests skip\n    84\t    (let [{:keys [exit]} (psh {:dir clone\n    85\t                               :out (io/file (str out \"/build-peer.log\"))\n    86\t                               :err :out\n    87\t                               :continue true}\n    88\t                              \"bb\" \"build:yin-repl-peer\")]\n    89\t      (log (str \"build-yin-repl-peer rc=\" exit))\n    90\t      (when-not (zero? exit) (fail! \"build:yin-repl-peer failed\")))\n    91\t    ;; per-subsystem cljd namespaces; the per-run files are the evidence\n    92\t    (let [lists (into {} (map (fn [s] [s (cljd-namespaces clone s)]) subs))\n    93\t          test-root (str (fs/canonicalize (str clone \"/test\")))\n    94\t          all (->> (file-seq (fs/file test-root))\n    95\t                   (filter #(re-find #\"_test\\.clj[cd]$\" (str %)))\n    96\t                   (map (fn [path]\n    97\t                          (-> (str path)\n    98\t                              (str/replace (str test-root \"/\") \"\")\n    99\t                              (str/replace #\"\\.clj[cd]$\" \"\")\n   100\t                              (str/replace \"/\" \".\")\n   101\t                              (str/replace \"_\" \"-\"))))\n   102\t                   set)\n   103\t          covered (apply set/union (map set (vals lists)))\n   104\t          uncovered (set/difference all covered)\n   105\t          lists (cond-> lists (seq uncovered)\n   106\t                        (assoc \"uncovered\" (vec uncovered)))]\n   107\t      (log (str \"all=\" (count all) \" covered=\" (count covered)\n   108\t                \" uncovered=\" (count uncovered)))\n   109\t      (doseq [[s nss] lists]\n   110\t        (spit (str out \"/ns-\" s \".txt\") (str/join \"\\n\" nss))))\n   111\t    ;; one full cljd compile\n   112\t    (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n   113\t          allns (->> (mapcat (fn [s]\n   114\t                               (some->> (str out \"/ns-\" s \".txt\")\n   115\t                                        slurp\n   116\t                                        str/split-lines\n   117\t                                        (remove str/blank?)))\n   118\t                             subs)\n   119\t                     ;; mapcat already flattened the subsystem lists. apply\n   120\t                     ;; concat would split each namespace string into chars.\n   121\t                     (concat (when (fs/exists? (str out \"/ns-uncovered.txt\"))\n   122\t                               (->> (slurp (str out \"/ns-uncovered.txt\"))\n   123\t                                    str/split-lines\n   124\t                                    (remove str/blank?))))\n   125\t                     distinct\n   126\t                     vec)\n   127\t          {:keys [exit]}\n   128\t          (apply psh {:dir clone\n   129\t                      :out (io/file (str out \"/compile.log\"))\n   130\t                      :err :out\n   131\t                      :continue true}\n   132\t                 \"clojure\" \"-M:clojuredart:cljd\" \"compile\" allns)]\n   133\t      (log (str \"compile-all rc=\" exit\n   134\t                \" secs=\" (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0) 1000)))\n   135\t      (when-not (zero? exit)\n   136\t        (fail! \"cljd compile failed\")\n   137\t        (System/exit @rc)))\n   138\t    ;; emit one shard dir per subsystem (residual included; failures fatal)\n   139\t    (let [dirs (atom [])\n   140\t          {:keys [continue]} nil]\n   141\t      (doseq [s (conj (vec subs) \"uncovered\")]\n   142\t        (let [f (str out \"/ns-\" s \".txt\")]\n   143\t          (when (.exists (fs/file f))\n   144\t            (let [nss (str/join \",\" (remove str/blank? (str/split-lines (slurp f))))\n   145\t                  d (str clone \"/build/cljd-agg-\" stamp \"-\" s)\n   146\t                  {:keys [exit]}\n   147\t                  (psh {:dir clone\n   148\t                        :out (io/file (str out \"/\" s \".emit.log\"))\n   149\t                        :err :out\n   150\t                        :continue true}\n   151\t                       \"bb\" \"src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\" \"--only\" nss\n   152\t                       \"--shard-dir\" d \"--no-compile\" \"--no-run\")]\n   153\t              (if (zero? exit)\n   154\t                (swap! dirs conj d)\n   155\t                (fail! (str \"shard \" s \" emission failed (rc=\" exit \")\")))))))\n   156\t      (if (empty? @dirs)\n   157\t        (fail! \"no shards emitted\")\n   158\t        ;; R3: ONE flutter invocation over every emitted directory — the\n   159\t        ;; project-wide build/test_cache kernel is touched by one process.\n   160\t        (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n   161\t              {:keys [exit]}\n   162\t              (apply psh {:dir clone\n   163\t                          :out (io/file (str out \"/all.log\"))\n   164\t                          :err :out\n   165\t                          :extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}\n   166\t                          :continue true}\n   167\t                     \"flutter\" \"test\" \"--concurrency\" (str conc) @dirs)\n   168\t              wall (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0) 1000)\n   169\t              verdict (some->> (slurp (str out \"/all.log\"))\n   170\t                               str/split-lines\n   171\t                               (filter #(re-find #\"All tests passed|Some tests failed\" %))\n   172\t                               last)]\n   173\t          (log (str \"flutter rc=\" exit \" wall=\" wall \"s \" (or verdict \"\")))\n   174\t          (when-not (zero? exit) (fail! (str \"flutter test rc=\" exit))))))\n   175\t    (log (str \"done rc=\" @rc))\n   176\t    (System/exit @rc)))\n   177\t\n   178\t\n   179\t(when (= *file* (System/getProperty \"babashka.file\"))\n   180\t  (apply -main *command-line-args*))\n     1\t(ns quick-sharded\n     2\t  \"Quick JVM execution using affected's unchanged selection and subsystem rules.\"\n     3\t  (:require\n     4\t    [affected :as a]\n     5\t    [babashka.fs :as fs]\n     6\t    [babashka.process :as p]\n     7\t    [clojure.set :as set]\n     8\t    [clojure.string :as str]))\n     9\t\n    10\t\n    11\t(defn changed-paths\n    12\t  \"Validate explicit/deleted paths just as affected does; otherwise use git.\"\n    13\t  [index {:keys [changed base]}]\n    14\t  (let [git-root (str/trim (:out (p/sh \"git\" \"rev-parse\" \"--show-toplevel\")))\n    15\t        _ (when-not (= git-root (str (fs/canonicalize \".\")))\n    16\t            (throw (ex-info \"run from the repo root\" {})))\n    17\t        paths (if (some? changed)\n    18\t                (mapv #(a/normalize-path git-root %) changed)\n    19\t                (a/changed-files base))\n    20\t        base (or base (str/trim (:out (p/sh \"git\" \"merge-base\" \"HEAD\" \"master\"))))\n    21\t        errors (concat\n    22\t                 (when (some nil? paths) [\"changed path outside the repo\"])\n    23\t                 (a/input-errors\n    24\t                   {:index index :changed (remove nil? paths)\n    25\t                    :explicit? (some? changed)\n    26\t                    :exists? #(or (fs/exists? %)\n    27\t                                  (zero? (:exit (p/sh \"git\" \"cat-file\" \"-e\"\n    28\t                                                      (str base \":\" %)))))}))]\n    29\t    (when (seq errors) (throw (ex-info (str/join \"\\n\" errors) {})))\n    30\t    (vec paths)))\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t(defn shard-plan\n    34\t  [index cfg nses]\n    35\t  (let [selected (set nses)\n    36\t        shards (into (sorted-map)\n    37\t                     (for [{:keys [name]} (:subsystems cfg)\n    38\t                           :let [owned (set/intersection\n    39\t                                         selected (a/select-subsystems index cfg [name]))]\n    40\t                           :when (seq owned)]\n    41\t                       [name (vec (sort owned))]))\n    42\t        ;; Like the shiva script's explicit uncovered shard: new namespaces\n    43\t        ;; absent from the registry still run. Never silently drop them.\n    44\t        residual (set/difference selected (set (mapcat val shards)))]\n    45\t    (cond-> shards\n    46\t      (seq residual) (assoc \"unmapped\" (vec (sort residual))))))\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn coverage\n    50\t  [selected shards]\n    51\t  (let [assigned (mapcat val shards)\n    52\t        covered (set assigned)]\n    53\t    {:selected (count (set selected)) :covered (count covered)\n    54\t     :uncovered (vec (sort (set/difference (set selected) covered)))\n    55\t     :unexpected (vec (sort (set/difference covered (set selected))))\n    56\t     :duplicates (vec (sort (keep (fn [[n c]] (when (> c 1) n))\n    57\t                                  (frequencies assigned))))}))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(defn check-coverage!\n    61\t  [selected shards out]\n    62\t  (fs/create-dirs out)\n    63\t  (let [{:keys [uncovered unexpected duplicates] :as result} (coverage selected shards)\n    64\t        write-nses #(spit (str out \"/\" %1 \".txt\")\n    65\t                          (apply str (map (fn [n] (str n \"\\n\")) %2)))]\n    66\t    (write-nses \"selected\" selected)\n    67\t    (write-nses \"covered\" (sort (set (mapcat val shards))))\n    68\t    (write-nses \"uncovered\" uncovered)\n    69\t    (doseq [[shard nses] shards] (write-nses (str \"ns-\" shard) nses))\n    70\t    (println (format \"Coverage: selected=%d covered=%d uncovered=%d unexpected=%d duplicates=%d\"\n    71\t                     (:selected result) (:covered result) (count uncovered)\n    72\t                     (count unexpected) (count duplicates)))\n    73\t    (when (some seq [uncovered unexpected duplicates])\n    74\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"FAIL: shard coverage mismatch \" (pr-str result)) result)))\n    75\t    result))\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(defn jvm-summary\n    79\t  \"Only a complete final runner summary counts; exit 0 alone is insufficient.\"\n    80\t  [text]\n    81\t  (when-let [[_ tests assertions failures errors]\n    82\t             (last (re-seq #\"(?m)^Ran (\\d+) tests containing (\\d+) assertions\\.\\r?\\n(\\d+) failures, (\\d+) errors\\.\"\n    83\t                           text))]\n    84\t    (zipmap [:tests :assertions :failures :errors]\n    85\t            (map parse-long [tests assertions failures errors]))))\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\t(defn run-shard!\n    89\t  [out [shard nses]]\n    90\t  (let [start (System/nanoTime)\n    91\t        log (str out \"/\" shard \".log\")\n    92\t        cmd (into [\"clojure\" \"-M:test\" \"-e\" \":slow\"]\n    93\t                  (mapcat #(vector \"-n\" (str %)) nses))\n    94\t        exit (:exit @(p/process cmd {:out (fs/file log) :err :out}))\n    95\t        summary (jvm-summary (slurp log))\n    96\t        row (merge {:shard shard :namespaces (count nses) :exit exit\n    97\t                    :seconds (/ (- (System/nanoTime) start) 1e9)\n    98\t                    :pass? (and (zero? exit) (some? summary)\n    99\t                                (zero? (+ (:failures summary) (:errors summary))))}\n   100\t                   summary)]\n   101\t    (println (format \"%s: exit=%d tests=%s assertions=%s failures=%s errors=%s %.3fs %s (log %s)\"\n   102\t                     shard exit (:tests row) (:assertions row) (:failures row)\n   103\t                     (:errors row) (:seconds row) (if (:pass? row) \"pass\" \"FAIL\") log))\n   104\t    row))\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\t(defn run-shards!\n   108\t  [out shards workers]\n   109\t  ;; Each worker owns a disjoint sequence; no more than N child JVMs.\n   110\t  (let [ordered (sort-by (comp - count val) shards)\n   111\t        jobs (mapv (fn [worker]\n   112\t                     (future\n   113\t                       (mapv #(run-shard! out %)\n   114\t                             (take-nth workers (drop worker ordered)))))\n   115\t                   (range (min workers (count shards))))]\n   116\t    (vec (mapcat deref jobs))))\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\t(defn parse-args\n   120\t  [args]\n   121\t  (loop [opts {:workers 4 :list? false} [arg & more] args]\n   122\t    (case arg\n   123\t      nil opts\n   124\t      (\"--list\" \"--dry-run\") (recur (assoc opts :list? true) more)\n   125\t      \"--workers\" (let [n (parse-long (or (first more) \"\"))]\n   126\t                    (when-not (and n (pos? n))\n   127\t                      (throw (ex-info \"--workers needs a positive integer\" {})))\n   128\t                    (recur (assoc opts :workers n) (rest more)))\n   129\t      \"--base\" (do (when (or (empty? more) (str/starts-with? (first more) \"--\"))\n   130\t                     (throw (ex-info \"--base needs a ref\" {})))\n   131\t                   (recur (assoc opts :base (first more)) (rest more)))\n   132\t      \"--changed\" (let [[files flags] (split-with #(not (str/starts-with? % \"--\")) more)]\n   133\t                    (when (empty? files)\n   134\t                      (throw (ex-info \"--changed needs at least one file\" {})))\n   135\t                    (recur (assoc opts :changed (vec files)) flags))\n   136\t      (throw (ex-info (str \"unknown option: \" arg) {})))))\n   137\t\n   138\t\n   139\t(defn verification-scope\n   140\t  \"Exit zero may mean feedback or a plan; only eligible executed gates complete.\"\n   141\t  [runner scope exit dry? details]\n   142\t  (merge {:type :verification-scope :runner runner :scope scope\n   143\t          :exit exit :dry-run? (boolean dry?)\n   144\t          :gate-complete? (boolean (and (zero? exit) (not dry?)\n   145\t                                        (#{:docs-whitespace :selected-quick-tri-host\n   146\t                                           :full-quick-tri-host} scope)\n   147\t                                        (empty? (:unchecked details))))}\n   148\t         details))\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\t(defn print-scope!\n   152\t  [record]\n   153\t  (prn record)\n   154\t  (:exit record))\n   155\t\n   156\t\n   157\t(defn- execute-quick!\n   158\t  [{:keys [workers list?] :as opts}]\n   159\t  (let [start (System/nanoTime)\n   160\t        index (a/scan-index)\n   161\t        cfg (or (a/load-subsystems-config)\n   162\t                (throw (ex-info \"missing src/dev/subsystems.edn\" {})))\n   163\t        selection (if (or (:changed opts) (:base opts))\n   164\t                    (a/select index (changed-paths index opts))\n   165\t                    {:tests (into #{} (comp (filter :test?) (map :ns)) index)})\n   166\t        nses (a/lane-tests index (:tests selection) :clj)\n   167\t        shards (shard-plan index cfg nses)\n   168\t        ;; Separate invocations never overwrite one another's evidence.\n   169\t        out (str \"target/profile/quick-sharded-\" (System/currentTimeMillis)\n   170\t                 \"-\" (subs (str (random-uuid)) 0 8))\n   171\t        cov (check-coverage! nses shards out)\n   172\t        prereqs (a/prerequisites index {:clj nses})]\n   173\t    (println \"Quick JVM only; workers=\" workers \"; logs:\" out)\n   174\t    (when (seq (:wide selection))\n   175\t      (println \"Wide selection: this runs the full JVM quick lane; G3 still requires bb test.\"))\n   176\t    (doseq [[shard tests] shards]\n   177\t      (println \"Shard\" shard \":\" (count tests) \"namespaces\"))\n   178\t    (when (contains? shards \"unmapped\")\n   179\t      (println \"Registry has unowned namespaces; running them explicitly in shard unmapped:\"\n   180\t               (str/join \", \" (get shards \"unmapped\"))))\n   181\t    (println \"Prerequisites:\" (str/join \", \" (sort (map name prereqs))))\n   182\t    (println \"G2 also requires the selected Node/Dart lanes; G3 bb test and applicable G4 remain mandatory.\")\n   183\t    (cond\n   184\t      (empty? nses)\n   185\t      (do (println \"REFUSED: 0 JVM namespaces selected; no JVM feedback executed.\")\n   186\t          (print-scope! (verification-scope :quick-sharded :jvm-feedback 1 list?\n   187\t                                            {:selected 0})))\n   188\t\n   189\t      list?\n   190\t      (print-scope! (verification-scope :quick-sharded :jvm-feedback 0 true\n   191\t                                        {:selected (count nses)}))\n   192\t\n   193\t      :else\n   194\t      (do\n   195\t        ;; All writers finish before any test JVM starts. No mutable output\n   196\t        ;; directory is shared with another worktree.\n   197\t        (doseq [task (concat (when (prereqs :build:yin-repl-node) [\"deps:npm\"])\n   198\t                             (keep #(when (prereqs %) (name %))\n   199\t                                   [:build:yin-repl-peer :build:yin-repl-node :gen:antlr]))]\n   200\t          (println \"Prerequisite\" task)\n;; Canonical Subsystems Definition for datom.world\n;; Longest-prefix match over Clojure/ClojureScript/ClojureDart namespaces.\n;; See docs/design/test.subsystems.md for architectural invariants and gate ladder.\n\n{:subsystems\n [;; Layer 0: Storage, Stream & Core Data Foundations\n  {:name \"dao.stream\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.stream\"]\n   :layer 0}\n\n  {:name \"dao.jing\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.jing\"]\n   :layer 0}\n\n  {:name \"dao.data\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.data\"]\n   :layer 0}\n\n  {:name \"dao.host\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.host\"]\n   :layer 0}\n\n  {:name \"dao.base\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.await\" \"dao.lease\" \"dao.pretty\" \"dao.datom\" \"dao.test-slow\"]\n   :layer 0}\n\n  ;; Layer 1: Space, GUI & Graphics\n  {:name \"dao.space\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.space\"]\n   :layer 1}\n\n  {:name \"dao.gui\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.gui\"]\n   :layer 1}\n\n  {:name \"dao.postgraphics\"\n   :prefixes [\"dao.postgraphics\"]\n   :layer 1}\n\n  ;; Layer 2: Virtual Machines & Execution\n  {:name \"yin.vm.ucf\"\n   :prefixes [\"yin.vm.ucf\"]\n   :layer 2}\n\n  {:name \"yin.vm\"\n   :prefixes [\"yin.vm\"]\n   :layer 2}\n\n  ;; Layer 3: Languages & Repl\n  {:name \"yin.repl\"\n   :prefixes [\"yin.repl\"]\n   :layer 3}\n\n  {:name \"yang.python\"\n   :prefixes [\"yang.python\" \"yang.antlr\"]\n   :layer 3}\n\n  {:name \"yang.typescript\"\n   :prefixes [\"yang.typescript\"]\n   :layer 3}\n\n  {:name \"yang.php\"\n   :prefixes [\"yang.php\"]\n   :layer 3}\n\n  {:name \"yang.base\"\n   :prefixes [\"yang.clojure\" \"yang.frontend\" \"yang.safepoint\"\n              \"yang.stage\" \"yang.tails\" \"yang.io\" \"yang.core\"]\n   :layer 3}\n\n  ;; Layer 4: Demos & World Applications\n  {:name \"demo\"\n   :prefixes [\"datomworld\" \"yin.demo\"]\n   :layer 4}\n\n  {:name \"world\"\n   :prefixes [\"world\"]\n   :layer 4}\n\n  ;; Development & Benchmarking Tooling\n  {:name \"dev\"\n   :prefixes [\"affected\" \"affected-test\" \"cljd-agg\"]\n   :layer :dev}\n\n  {:name \"bench\"\n   :prefixes [\"bench\"]\n   :layer :bench}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"One policy claim is already off: 03:00 and 17:00 are 14 hours apart, then 10 hours apart. Detection also includes test runtime, so the stated 12-hour worst case is too low. I’m checking whether the scheduled runs and coverage records support the other guarantees.\n"}}
