{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' src/dev/cljd_agg.clj && cat src/cljc/dao/test_slow.cljc && cat shadow-cljs.edn && sed -n '1,100p' collab/1793514000000-reviewer-node-shard-diagnosis.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"(ns cljd-agg\n  \"Dart test runner that aggregates the generated test files.\n\n   `flutter test` loads every generated *_test.dart separately (about 7.5 s\n   each). This runner compiles the test namespaces through the cljd tool,\n   groups the generated files into a few shard files that import them and call\n   each `main`, and runs `flutter test` on the shards only. Shards live under\n   build/, never under test/, so a plain `cljd test` never runs them twice.\n\n   Run with babashka:\n     bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj [--slow-only | --slow-regex | --only NS,NS...]\n   --slow-only restricts the run to the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard.\n   A namespace in that set with no generated Dart file is fatal.\n   --only compiles and runs only the given test namespaces (bb test:changed,\n   bb test:sub); one with no generated Dart file is fatal too, EXCEPT a\n   JVM-only namespace: one whose every deftest sits behind a reader\n   conditional that excludes ClojureDart (for example\n   dao.data.sorted-user-type-test). The cljd tool compiles such a namespace as\n   a plain library (lib/cljd-out/<ns>.dart exists) and emits no test file;\n   that is reported and skipped, never fatal. A namespace that produced\n   neither file is still fatal.\n   --slow-regex prints, for bb.edn, an anchored alternation of those\n   namespaces with its dots already escaped for embedding in an EDN string\n   (shadow-cljs --config-merge); it is not a ready-to-use regex. It exits 1\n   when no namespace uses the guard, so a slow lane cannot be vacuous.\n   DATOM_SLOW_TESTS is inherited from the environment.\"\n  (:require\n    [babashka.fs :as fs]\n    [babashka.process :as p]\n    [clojure.string :as str]))\n\n\n(def test-root \"test\")\n(def out-root \"test/cljd-out\")\n(def shard-dir \"build/cljd-agg\")\n(def max-shards 8)\n\n\n(defn- ns-of\n  \"The namespace declared by the first ns form of `file`.\"\n  [file]\n  (second (re-find #\"\\(ns\\s+\\^?(?:\\{[^}]*\\}\\s+)?([^\\s\\)]+)\" (slurp file))))\n\n\n(defn- source-files\n  []\n  (->> (file-seq (fs/file test-root))\n       (filter #(re-find #\"_test\\.clj[cd]$\" (str %)))\n       (remove #(str/includes? (str %) \"cljd-out\"))\n       (map str)\n       sort))\n\n\n(defn- test-namespaces\n  \"Distinct: a namespace with both a .cljc and a .cljd source (for example\n   dao.stream.cbor-test) has one generated Dart file, which must run once.\"\n  []\n  (distinct (keep ns-of (source-files))))\n\n\n(defn- slow-namespaces\n  \"Namespaces whose source uses dao.test-slow/guard, derived from the tree.\"\n  []\n  (->> (source-files)\n       (filter #(re-find #\"slow/guard\" (slurp %)))\n       (keep ns-of)\n       distinct\n       sort))\n\n\n(defn- dart-file\n  \"Generated file path for namespace `ns-name`.\"\n  [ns-name]\n  (str out-root \"/\" (str/replace ns-name \".\" \"/\") \"_test.dart\"))\n\n\n(defn- lib-file\n  \"Library file the cljd tool writes for a namespace with no Dart tests.\"\n  [ns-name]\n  (str \"lib/cljd-out/\" (str/replace ns-name \".\" \"/\") \".dart\"))\n\n\n(defn jvm-only?\n  \"True when `ns-name` compiled to a library but produced no Dart test file:\n   it has no ClojureDart tests (a JVM-only namespace), as opposed to not\n   having compiled at all.\"\n  [ns-name]\n  (and (not (fs/exists? (dart-file ns-name)))\n       (fs/exists? (lib-file ns-name))))\n\n\n(defn- run!*\n  [& args]\n  (let [{:keys [exit]} (apply p/shell {:continue true} args)]\n    exit))\n\n\n(defn compile-tests\n  \"Compile every test namespace through the cljd tool.\"\n  [namespaces]\n  (let [exit (apply run!* \"clojure\" \"-M:clojuredart:cljd\" \"compile\"\n                    namespaces)]\n    (when-not (zero? exit)\n      (println \"cljd compile failed, exit\" exit)\n      (System/exit exit))))\n\n\n(defn shard\n  \"Greedy balanced partition of `files` into `n` groups by file size.\n   Deterministic: ties are broken by path.\"\n  [files n]\n  (let [sized (sort-by (juxt (comp - fs/size) identity) files)\n        init  (vec (repeat n {:size 0 :files []}))]\n    (->> sized\n         (reduce (fn [shards f]\n                   (let [i (first (first (sort-by\n                                           (juxt (comp :size second) first)\n                                           (map-indexed vector shards))))]\n                     (-> shards\n                         (update-in [i :size] + (fs/size f))\n                         (update-in [i :files] conj f))))\n                 init)\n         (map (comp sort :files))\n         (remove empty?))))\n\n\n(defn- shard-source\n  \"Dart source of an aggregator importing `files` and calling each main.\n   Imports are relative to `shard-dir`.\"\n  [files shard-dir]\n  (let [rel (fn [f]\n              (str (fs/relativize (fs/absolutize shard-dir)\n                                  (fs/absolutize f))))]\n    (str \"// Generated by src/dev/cljd_agg.clj; do not edit.\\n\"\n         (apply str\n                (map-indexed (fn [i f]\n                               (str \"import '\" (rel f) \"' as m\" i \";\\n\"))\n                             files))\n         \"\\nvoid main() {\\n\"\n         (apply str\n                (map-indexed (fn [i _] (str \"  m\" i \".main();\\n\")) files))\n         \"}\\n\")))\n\n\n(defn write-shards!\n  \"Emit the aggregator files under `shard-dir` (build/cljd-agg by default;\n   --shard-dir overrides, which lets dart-shard.sh run one directory per\n   subsystem as parallel flutter processes). Returns the shard paths.\"\n  ([files] (write-shards! files shard-dir))\n  ([files shard-dir]\n   (fs/delete-tree shard-dir)\n   (fs/create-dirs shard-dir)\n   (let [n (min max-shards\n                (.availableProcessors (Runtime/getRuntime))\n                (count files))]\n     (vec (map-indexed\n            (fn [i group]\n              (let [path (format \"%s/shard_%d_test.dart\" shard-dir i)]\n                (spit path (shard-source group shard-dir))\n                path))\n            (shard files n))))))\n\n\n(defn -main\n  [& args]\n  (when (some #{\"--slow-regex\"} args)\n    (when (empty? (slow-namespaces))\n      (println \"No namespace uses dao.test-slow/guard.\")\n      (System/exit 1))\n    (println (str \"^(\" (str/join \"|\" (map #(str/replace % \".\" \"\\\\\\\\.\")\n                                          (slow-namespaces)))\n                  \")$\"))\n    (System/exit 0))\n  (let [slow-only? (some #{\"--slow-only\"} args)\n        only       (when (some #{\"--only\"} args)\n                     (let [v (second (drop-while #(not= \"--only\" %) args))]\n                       (vec (remove str/blank? (str/split (str v) #\",\")))))\n        shard-dir  (or (when (some #{\"--shard-dir\"} args)\n                         (second (drop-while #(not= \"--shard-dir\" %) args)))\n                       shard-dir)\n        no-compile? (some #{\"--no-compile\"} args)\n        no-run?    (some #{\"--no-run\"} args)\n        wanted     (cond only only\n                         slow-only? (slow-namespaces)\n                         :else (test-namespaces))]\n    (when (empty? wanted)\n      (println \"No test namespaces selected.\")\n      (System/exit 1))\n    (when-not no-compile?\n      (compile-tests (or only (test-namespaces))))\n    (let [files (filter fs/exists? (map dart-file wanted))\n          missing (remove (comp fs/exists? dart-file) wanted)]\n      (when (seq missing)\n        (let [jvm-only (if (and only (not slow-only?))\n                         (filter jvm-only? missing)\n                         [])\n              fatal (remove (set jvm-only) missing)]\n          (when (seq jvm-only)\n            (println \"JVM-only namespaces (compiled, no Dart tests; skipped):\"\n                     (str/join \", \" jvm-only)))\n          (when (seq fatal)\n            (println \"No generated Dart test for:\" (str/join \", \" fatal))\n            (when (or slow-only? only)\n              (System/exit 1)))))\n      (when (empty? files)\n        (println \"No generated test files found.\")\n        (System/exit 1))\n      (let [shards (write-shards! files shard-dir)]\n        (if no-run?\n          (do (println (format \"Emitted %d test files in %d shards under %s\"\n                               (count files) (count shards) shard-dir))\n              (System/exit 0))\n          (do (println (format \"Running %d test files in %d shards\"\n                               (count files) (count shards)))\n              (let [exit (try (apply run!* \"flutter\" \"test\"\n                                     \"--concurrency\" (str (count shards))\n                                     shards)\n                              (finally (fs/delete-tree shard-dir)))]\n                (System/exit exit))))))))\n\n\n(when (= *file* (System/getProperty \"babashka.file\"))\n  (apply -main *command-line-args*))\ncat: src/cljc/dao/test_slow.cljc: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The hourly cron entries are installed on both hosts. The run evidence is less reassuring: the completed JVM slow run has seven red namespaces, and the latest paired JVM run has quick and slow failures. Shiva’s paired run is still blocked in Node, with Dart queued behind it.\n\nThere is also a pairing risk: both hosts fire at the same minute, but Jupiter accepts any pin dated today. At 17:00 it could read the 03:00 pin before Shiva publishes the new one.\n"}}
