{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '128,210p' collab/1793514000000-reviewer-node-shard-diagnosis.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md && sed -n '1,260p' src/dev/test_routed.clj && rg -n 'stream|dht|slow|deftest' test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj test/yin/vm/linker/cross_host_transfer_test.clj test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.clj | head -85\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '128,210p' collab/1793514000000-reviewer-node-shard-diagnosis.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md && sed -n '1,260p' src/dev/test_routed.clj && rg -n 'stream|dht|slow|deftest' test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj test/yin/vm/linker/cross_host_transfer_test.clj test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.clj | head -85\"","aggregated_output":"\nA second run collected an in-memory CPU profile over 60 seconds:\n\n```text\nTotal samples:             55,403\nGarbage-collector samples:  1,246  (2.25%)\nHeap used at end:         842,763,328 bytes\nVmHWM:                     1,412,872 kB\nVmSwap:                            0 kB\n```\n\nTop sampled functions included query execution `step`, `unify-slots`, `run-comp`, and execution-budget `charge`. Late GC traces showed:\n\n```text\n841.6 (908.5) -> 777.6 (908.5) MB\naverage mu = 0.989, current mu = 0.979\n```\n\nThat is inconsistent with heap-ceiling GC thrash **during this reproduction**. It demonstrates substantial computation even before failure dumps are printed. It does not prove an infinite loop, nor reproduce the already-killed workers’ final hours.\n\nThe giant dumps and buffering are additional problems. The last logged failed assertion is `(is (vm/halted? child))`; the default reporter formats its actual value using `pr-str`, potentially traversing a huge VM state. Meanwhile, the driver uses buffered `io/writer`s. Both observed file sizes are multiples of 8,192 bytes. A mid-line tail therefore cannot reliably locate the currently executing expression.\n\n4. **Per-shard builds are a possible optimization, but the proposed command is incorrect and does not address the confirmed failure.**\n\nI checked the packaged **shadow-cljs 3.3.5 source**:\n\n- **`:output-to` through `--config-merge`: yes.**\n- **`:ns-regexp` through `--config-merge`: yes.**\n- **`:cache-root` through that build-level merge: no.** The runtime’s global cache root and build cache directory are established before the CLI build-config merge. The official documentation explicitly makes `:cache-root` global. [Shadow configuration documentation](https://github.com/shadow-cljs/shadow-cljs.github.io/blob/master/docs/build-config.adoc)\n\nConsequently, your proposed commands still use the same `test/dev` cache and default runtime output directory. Separate `node-tests-<s>.js` launchers would reference shared runtime files, including runner code that subsequent compiles can overwrite.\n\nIf smaller artifacts are subsequently justified, use **distinct build IDs**, for example:\n\n```clojure\n{:builds\n {:test-dao-jing\n  {:target :node-test\n   :namespaces [dao.jing-test dao.jing.cbor-test]\n   :output-to \"target/node-tests-dao-jing.js\"\n   :autorun false}}}\n```\n\nDistinct build IDs receive separate build caches and default runtime directories. The pinned source supports explicit `:namespaces`; this also avoids regex escaping and anchoring mistakes.\n\nTwo qualifications matter:\n\n- Selection includes the chosen namespaces’ dependency closure. Tests that require other test namespaces can bring those tests into the artifact. The runner’s inventory macro collects test vars from analyzed namespaces.\n- **`--test=<list>` still works** and remains useful to restrict execution to the intended shard.\n\nI could not reproduce the alleged cache leakage without compiling, which would violate the read-only constraint. Source inspection shows that `:ns-regexp` regenerates test entries during resolution; previously compiled files remaining on disk alone do not prove that those namespaces are still imported.\n\nFor cost, preserved summaries repeatedly show **22–23 seconds for warm full compiles**. I did not measure a cold isolated build or fourteen per-shard builds. Fourteen comparable warm invocations would total roughly five minutes, but that is arithmetic, not a measured per-shard result.\n\nMy recommended order is:\n\n1. Verify the corrected selector, including actual executed namespace names and completion summaries.\n2. Keep one compile initially and measure genuine shard peaks and runtimes.\n3. Investigate the Python fixture/publication/query path and bound failure formatting.\n4. Introduce distinct per-shard builds if their measured startup or memory savings justify compilation costs.\n\nIncreasing `--max-old-space-size` has no demonstrated benefit from these measurements. Fewer workers or distributing work across both hosts can control aggregate load, but cannot repair ignored selection or accelerate one pathological test. Shadow’s Node output implementation also explicitly requires one module, making `:modules` an unsuitable direct fix here.\n\n5. **The 30,297-second result is not reliable evidence of a completed suite.**\n\nThe preserved files are:\n\n```text\n~/ci/nightly-results/20261031-0223-summary.txt\n~/ci/nightly-results/20261031-0223-cljs-full.log\n```\n\nThe summary records `cljs-full rc=0 secs=30297`. However, the test log:\n\n- contains numerous failures and errors;\n- reaches the same linked-prelude tests;\n- has **no `Ran … tests` summary**;\n- ends mid-dump before shadow prints `Build completed … 30267.97s`.\n\nShadow’s autorun waits for Node and records its exit status internally; the compile command’s success is not reliable test-success evidence. The runner also calls `process.exit()` immediately at end-of-tests. Node documents that pending asynchronous stdout writes can be lost on exit, so missing output alone cannot prove where execution stopped. [Node process documentation](https://nodejs.org/download/release/v25.6.0/docs/api/process.html#process_exit_code)\n\nThus the 8.4-hour and 10-hour observations are plausibly related to the same expensive slow-test path, compounded by poor output visibility. I cannot establish that their terminal behavior was identical. **The confirmed causes are ineffective sharding and costly slow-test computation; late-stage GC thrash in the killed processes remains unverified.**(ns test-routed\n  \"Explicit policy dispatch; wide changes always execute the full tri-host gate.\"\n  (:require\n    [affected :as a]\n    [babashka.process :as p]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [quick-sharded :as quick]))\n\n\n(defn docs-only?\n  [path]\n  ;; Executable documentation and test resources are ordinary affected input.\n  (and (not (str/starts-with? path \"test/resources/\"))\n       (boolean (re-find #\"\\.(?:md|txt|rst)$\" path))))\n\n\n(defn toolchain?\n  [path]\n  (or (= :wide (a/classify path))\n      (boolean (re-find #\"(?:^|/)(?:[^/]*toolchain[^/]*|Dockerfile[^/]*|Makefile)$\" path))\n      (str/starts-with? path \".github/workflows/\")\n      (str/starts-with? path \"scripts/\")))\n\n\n(defn foundation?\n  [index cfg path]\n  (let [ns-sym (or (:ns (some #(when (= path (:path %)) %) index))\n                   (a/path->ns path))\n        sub (when ns-sym (a/match-subsystem cfg ns-sym))]\n    (and (#{:code} (a/classify path))\n         (or (= 0 (:layer sub))\n             (and ns-sym\n                  (some #(let [n (str ns-sym)]\n                           (or (= n %) (str/starts-with? n (str % \".\"))\n                               (str/starts-with? n (str % \"-\"))))\n                        [\"yang.clojure\" \"yang.php\" \"yang.typescript\" \"yang.python\"]))))))\n\n\n(defn route\n  [index cfg paths]\n  (cond\n    (some toolchain? paths) {:class :toolchain :command [\"bb\" \"test\"]}\n    (and (seq paths) (every? docs-only? paths))\n    {:class :docs :paths paths :command (into [\"git\" \"diff\" \"--check\" \"HEAD\" \"--\"] paths)}\n    (some #(foundation? index cfg %) paths)\n    {:class :foundation\n     :command (into [\"bb\" \"test:quick-sharded\" \"--changed\"] paths)}\n    ;; A non-doc change with no statically selected tests is not a green gate.\n    (empty? (:tests (a/select index paths)))\n    {:class :unselected :command [\"bb\" \"test\"]}\n    :else {:class :leaf :command (into [\"bb\" \"test:changed\" \"--changed\"] paths)}))\n\n\n(defn dispatch!\n  [{:keys [class command paths]} dry?]\n  (println (str \"Dispatch [\" (name class) \"]: \" (str/join \" \" command)\n                (when (#{:toolchain :unselected} class)\n                  \" (full quick tri-host; success required)\")\n                (when dry? \" (DRY RUN; no gate executed)\")))\n  (when (= class :foundation)\n    (println \"JVM feedback only: G2 still needs test:changed:cljs and test:changed:cljd for these files; G3/G4 remain required.\"))\n  (let [scope (case class\n                :docs :docs-whitespace\n                :foundation :jvm-feedback\n                :leaf :selected-quick-tri-host\n                :full-quick-tri-host)\n        report! (fn [scope exit details]\n                  (quick/print-scope! (quick/verification-scope :test-routed scope exit dry? details)))]\n    (try\n      (if dry?\n        (report! scope 0 {})\n        (let [unchecked (when (= class :docs)\n                          (let [{:keys [exit out]}\n                                @(p/process (into [\"git\" \"ls-files\" \"-z\" \"--\"] paths)\n                                            {:out :string :err :string})]\n                            (when-not (zero? exit)\n                              (throw (ex-info \"git ls-files failed: docs scope unknown\" {:exit exit})))\n                            (let [tracked (set (str/split out #\"\\u0000\"))]\n                              (vec (remove tracked paths)))))\n              _ (doseq [path unchecked] (println (str path \": unchecked (untracked)\")))\n              exit (:exit @(p/process command {:inherit true}))]\n          (if (and (= class :leaf) (= a/wide-exit exit))\n            (do (println \"Dispatch [wide exit 2]: bb test (full quick tri-host; success required)\")\n                (report! :full-quick-tri-host\n                         (:exit @(p/process [\"bb\" \"test\"] {:inherit true})) {}))\n            (report! scope exit (if (= class :docs) {:unchecked unchecked} {})))))\n      (catch Exception ex\n        (report! scope 1 {})\n        (throw ex)))))\n\n\n(defn -main\n  [& args]\n  (try\n    (let [dry? (boolean (some #{\"--dry-run\" \"--list\"} args))\n          paths (vec (remove #{\"--dry-run\" \"--list\"} args))\n          _ (when (some #(str/starts-with? % \"--\") paths)\n              (throw (ex-info \"usage: bb test:routed [--dry-run] <changed-files...>\" {})))\n          index (a/scan-index)\n          ;; No positional args means the same git change set as test:changed.\n          paths (quick/changed-paths index (when (seq paths) {:changed paths}))\n          _ (when (empty? paths)\n              (throw (ex-info \"no changed files: no gate dispatched\" {})))\n          cfg (or (a/load-subsystems-config)\n                  (throw (ex-info \"missing src/dev/subsystems.edn\" {})))]\n      (System/exit (dispatch! (route index cfg paths) dry?)))\n    (catch Exception ex\n      (binding [*out* *err*] (println (ex-message ex)))\n      (System/exit 1))))\n\n\n(when (= *file* (System/getProperty \"babashka.file\"))\n  (apply -main *command-line-args*))\nrg: test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.clj: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ntest/yin/vm/linker/cross_host_transfer_test.clj:4:   stream envelopes cross Transit pipes between two ring compositions.\ntest/yin/vm/linker/cross_host_transfer_test.clj:10:            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\ntest/yin/vm/linker/cross_host_transfer_test.clj:14:            [dao.stream :as stream]\ntest/yin/vm/linker/cross_host_transfer_test.clj:15:            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\ntest/yin/vm/linker/cross_host_transfer_test.clj:16:            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\ntest/yin/vm/linker/cross_host_transfer_test.clj:17:            [dao.stream.transit :as transit]\ntest/yin/vm/linker/cross_host_transfer_test.clj:43:  (:dao.stream/handle\ntest/yin/vm/linker/cross_host_transfer_test.clj:44:    (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/t