\\\\n233:   - **The Linux version script is unbuilt and untested.**\\\\\\\\n234: - **Test seams behind a CMake option:**\\\\\\\\n235:   - `option(JOLT_PARSER_TEST_SEAMS … OFF)` gates `jolt_parser_inject_fault`, the fault branches themselves (`maybe_fault`, `fail_handler_malloc`), and the new stats/thread/heap seams.\\\\\\\\n236:   - `bb build:jolt-native` now builds both variants: `jolt-parser/` (seams ON, what the probes and harnesses load) and `jolt-parser-release/` (CMake default, OFF). It records both, with their exported symbol lists, in `build-record.edn`.\\\\\\\\n237:   - The round-1 probe and the parity harness look the seam up (`ffi/find-symbol`). They print `SKIP … built without JOLT_PARSER_TEST_SEAMS` when it is absent; the probe shows this against the release build through `JOLT_PARSER_PROBE_LIB`.\\\\\\\\n238: - **Nonallocating failure paths are kept:** `message()` is unchanged apart from `fail_handler_malloc()`, and `Oversize` and the busy refusal allocate nothing.\\\\\\\\n239: - **Export layout version entry** (cmd G2/H3): new `jolt_parser_export_layout_version()` answers 2. `cst.jolt` checks it at load and refuses a library that writes another layout. The buffer still carries its version, and the decoder still checks that too.\\\\\\\\n240: - **dylibs:** test `2913f3ed9815f68041ca99fd9324eb2d0043bf761396640d0bb043c437d5413e`, release `9361c17641c57139dfab61d59b0e80ef9c7071010a7282f79ee362b3c973c9fd`. Both depend only on `libc++` and `libSystem`.\\\\\\\\n241: - **ABI change:** `jolt_parser_export` now takes the worker first. The JPX1 layout itself is unchanged (version 2).\\\\\\\\n242: \\\\\\\\n243: ## Commands (in the worktree) and exit codes\\\\\\\\n244: \\\\\\\\n245: Long runs: the tool moves any foreground command past 600 s to the background and stops it 10 minutes later. My first full stack run (part 1: parens, list, call), a `unary not` batch and two sanitize runs were stopped that way. The final full stack run and the 50-cycle sanitize run were then launched with `run_in_background` and a long timeout, and I waited for their completion notifications. No other command ran in the background.\\\\\\\\n246: \\\\\\\\n247: | command | exit | log |\\\\\\\\n248: |---|---|---|\\\\\\\\n249: | `bb build:jolt-native` (first: macro clash, Mach `TRUE/FALSE` vs generated token names, so the includes were moved after the generated headers; later builds after the BOM fix) | 1, then 0, 0 | `r4-build.log` |\\\\\\\\n250: | `jolt … src/dev/jolt_j0c_workers.clj` (the first runs failed the busy check on a test race; the test was fixed) | 1, 1, then 0 | `r4-workers-final.log` |\\\\\\\\n251: | `bb src/dev/jolt_j0c_stack.clj` (final, all shapes, with the 20 s per-parse cap added after unary took about 104 s at 1,024 and a run had to be stopped) | 0 | `r4-stack.log`, `build/j0c/r4/stack-budget.edn` |\\\\\\\\n252: | `jolt … src/dev/jolt_j0c_gc.clj` | 0 | `r4-gc.log` |\\\\\\\\n253: | `clojure -M:dev -m jolt-j0c-oracle input`; `clojure -M:dev -m jolt-j0c-oracle` (round-2 oracle regenerated, SHA-256 unchanged) | 0, 0 | `r4-input-oracle.log`, `r4-oracle-rerun.log` |\\\\\\\\n254: | parity harness (`jolt -Srepro -Sdeps '{:aliases {:j0c-probe-stub {:extra-paths [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"src/dev/jolt-j0c-probe-stub\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]}}}' -M:jolt:j0c-probe-stub src/dev/jolt_j0c_parity.clj`). Intermediate runs: an NPE in the E1 checker on the BOM entry (fixed: nil-safe); `(ffi/null)` misuse (fixed). Final: 132 PASS | 1, 1, then 0 | `r4-parity-final.log` |\\\\\\\\n255: | `jolt … src/dev/jolt_j0c_cycles.clj 5000` and `… 20000` | 0, 0 | `r4-cycles.log`, `r4-cycles-20000.log` |\\\\\\\\n256: | `bb src/dev/jolt_j0c_sanitize.clj 50` (earlier: a missing `support/Utf8.h` include, exit 1; a 200-cycle run with a 200,000-statement oversize case was stopped as too slow under ASan, and the case was replaced by one large string token) | 0 | `r4-sanitize.log` |\\\\\\\\n257: | `jolt -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj` (test build; then with `JOLT_PARSER_PROBE_LIB=…/jolt-parser-release/…`) | 0 (11 PASS), 0 (7 PASS + SKIP) | `r4-probe-r1.log`, `r4-probe-r1-release.log` |\\\\\\\\n258: | `bb smoke:jolt` | 0 | `r4-smoke.log` |\\\\\\\\n259: | `mise exec -- cljstyle check` on every changed Clojure/EDN file | 0 | n/a |\\\\\\\\n260: | `clojure -M:kondo --lint` on the dev scripts | known classes only: `defcfn` names unresolved, `cst/*` resolved against the JVM `cst.clj`, a stale `validate!` arity, and the pre-existing `run!` warning in `jolt_native.clj` | n/a |\\\\\\\\n261: \\\\\\\\n262: ## Files\\\\\\\\n263: \\\\\\\\n264: **Modified:**\\\\\\\\n265: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/native/jolt-parser/jolt_parser.cpp`: workers, the −5 busy guard, `SourceStream` (BOM), the bound enforced while growing, `TEST_SEAMS` gating, the stats/thread/heap seams, the export layout version entry.\\\\\\\\n266: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/native/jolt-parser/CMakeLists.txt`: the `JOLT_PARSER_TEST_SEAMS` option, the exported-symbols list / version script.\\\\\\\\n267: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt`: native worker handle, `close-worker`, worker-taking `export-records`, the layout version check at load.\\\\\\\\n268: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_native.clj`: builds the test and release variants, records their exported symbols.\\\\\\\\n269: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_parser_probe.clj`: the fault checks skip without the seam; `JOLT_PARSER_PROBE_LIB`.\\\\\\\\n270: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_j0c_parity.clj`: workers closed, the input-policy section, a nil-safe E1 checker, the fault checks skip without the seam.\\\\\\\\n271: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_j0c_oracle.clj`: the `input` mode.\\\\\\\\n272: \\\\\\\\n273: **Added:**\\\\\\\\n274: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/native/jolt-parser/exports.darwin`\\\\\\\\n275: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/native/jolt-parser/exports.linux`\\\\\\\\n276: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/native/jolt-parser/sanitize/CMakeLists.txt`\\\\\\\\n277: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/native/jolt-parser/sanitize/harness.cpp`\\\\\\\\n278: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_j0c_workers.clj`\\\\\\\\n279: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_j0c_stack.clj`\\\\\\\\n280: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_j0c_stack_child.clj`\\\\\\\\n281: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_j0c_gc.clj`\\\\\\\\n282: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_j0c_cycles.clj`\\\\\\\\n283: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/dev/jolt_j0c_sanitize.clj`\\\\\\\\n284: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/test/yang/python/antlr/fixtures/jolt_j0c_input_corpus.edn`\\\\\\\\n285: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/test/yang/python/antlr/fixtures/jolt_j0c_input_oracle.edn` (written by the JVM)\\\\\\\\n286: \\\\\\\\n287: **Untouched:** the round-2/3 corpus and oracle, the manifest and its recorded digests, `docs/design`, the shared exporter and packet code, and dao.stream, dao.data, dao.jing and yin.vm.\\\\\\\\n288: \\\\\\\\n289: Report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792500314000-engineer-jolt-j0c-r4.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md\\\\\\\"}]}],\\\\\\\"meta\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"messageId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"e55fc800-60e8-4261-9cb0-055a7dfc3af3\\\\\\\"}},{\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"assistant\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"thinking\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"thinking\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Okay, now let me adversarially read through the C++ — worker ownership, busy guard, SourceStream BOM fix, Oversize, seam gating, non-allocating paths. The file is currently probably around 700 lines. Going to read it.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"signature\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Now the wrapper source, the key adversarial target.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool_use\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"call_ac06bcfc4a574f019818ed5f\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"read_file\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"input\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"file_path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/native/jolt-parser/jolt_parser.cpp\\\\\\\"}}],\\\\\\\"meta\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"model\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"createdAt\\\\\\\":1792508093589,\\\\\\\"messageId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"59fe5c36-19ff-47e7-b381-e0c9d2e66b4c\\\\\\\"}},{\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"user\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tool_use_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"call_ac06bcfc4a574f019818ed5f\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Read 1/1 file, 694 lines\\\\\\\\n1: // jolt-parser: the extern \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"C\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" boundary between jolt and the ANTLR4 C++\\\\\\\\n2: // Python3 parser (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §7.3).\\\\\\\\n3: //\\\\\\\\n4: // J0c round 1 probe surface. Bytes in, bytes out: the caller passes UTF-8\\\\\\\\n5: // source by pointer and length and receives one private marshalling buffer,\\\\\\\\n6: // which it copies and returns through jolt_parser_free. No C++ class, layout\\\\\\\\n7: // or exception crosses this boundary; every entry catches std::exception and\\\\\\\\n8: // (...) and answers an explicit status. This is process-local marshalling (like\\\\\\\\n9: // a sockaddr), not a value codec: it never enters a stream. Packets are built\\\\\\\\n10: // by the shared jolt/Clojure exporter from these records, never here.\\\\\\\\n11: //\\\\\\\\n12: // Buffer layout, all integers little-endian:\\\\\\\\n13: //\\\\\\\\n14: //   magic   \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"JPT1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n15: //   u32     layout version (1)\\\\\\\\n16: //   u32     status (0 ok, 1 syntax errors)\\\\\\\\n17: //   u32     rule-name count R,     then R  x (u32 len, UTF-8 bytes)\\\\\\\\n18: //   u32     symbolic-name count S, then S  x (u32 len, UTF-8 bytes)\\\\\\\\n19: //   u32     node count N, then N preorder records:\\\\\\\\n20: //             u8  kind (0 rule, 1 token)\\\\\\\\n21: //             rule:  u32 rule index, u32 child count\\\\\\\\n22: //             token: i32 token type, u32 start, u32 stop (code-point indexes,\\\\\\\\n23: //                    0xFFFFFFFF = none), u32 text len, UTF-8 text\\\\\\\\n24: //   u32     error count E, then E x (u32 line, u32 column, u32 len, UTF-8 msg)\\\\\\\\n25: //\\\\\\\\n26: // Status codes returned by jolt_parser_parse:\\\\\\\\n27: //    0  parsed, buffer written (status field says whether errors occurred)\\\\\\\\n28: //   -1  invalid arguments\\\\\\\\n29: //   -2  C++ exception (std::exception); *out holds its message, UTF-8\\\\\\\\n30: //   -3  unknown exception\\\\\\\\n31: // On -2/-3 the message buffer is built without anything that can throw\\\\\\\\n32: // (strlen/malloc/memcpy only); if even that malloc fails, *out stays NULL and\\\\\\\\n33: // only the status reports the failure. No handler can throw.\\\\\\\\n34: //\\\\\\\\n35: //   -4  output would exceed the bound (64 MiB), checked while the buffer\\\\\\\\n36: //       grows, so an oversize answer is never built in full\\\\\\\\n37: //   -5  the worker is in use by another call (a worker serves one thread at\\\\\\\\n38: //       a time; this call did nothing)\\\\\\\\n39: //\\\\\\\\n40: // jolt_parser_parse (J0c round 1) recognizes with the generated static\\\\\\\\n41: // caches. jolt_parser_export takes a worker (§7.4, round 4): an opaque handle\\\\\\\\n42: // from jolt_parser_worker_new that owns its lexer and parser DFA vectors and\\\\\\\\n43: // PredictionContextCaches; each call installs fresh Lexer/ParserATNSimulators\\\\\\\\n44: // over them in place of the generated defaults (which point at the static\\\\\\\\n45: // caches) before recognition. The ATNs are the generated immutable tables and\\\\\\\\n46: // stay shared. jolt_parser_worker_free disposes the handle.\\\\\\\\n47: //\\\\\\\\n48: // TEST SEAMS, compiled only with -DJOLT_PARSER_TEST_SEAMS=ON (CMake option,\\\\\\\\n49: // default OFF): jolt_parser_inject_fault makes the next parses fail\\\\\\\\n50: // deterministically so the containment paths can be shown without\\\\\\\\n51: // exhausting memory; jolt_parser_static_cache_stats and\\\\\\\\n52: // jolt_parser_worker_cache_stats count cache contents;\\\\\\\\n53: // jolt_parser_thread_info reports the calling thread's stack;\\\\\\\\n54: // jolt_parser_heap_in_use reports malloc's bytes in use.\\\\\\\\n55: //\\\\\\\\n56: // jolt_parser_export answers the records the jolt yang.antlr.cst adapter\\\\\\\\n57: // hands to the shared exporter (§7.3). Indexes are i32, -1 for ANTLR's\\\\\\\\n58: // \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"none\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (INVALID_INDEX, a stop before a zero-width start), as the JVM\\\\\\\\n59: // reports them. Its layout (version from jolt_parser_export_layout_version):\\\\\\\\n60: //\\\\\\\\n61: //   magic   \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"JPX1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n62: //   u32     layout version (2; 2 added the offending token type)\\\\\\\\n63: //   u32     status (0 ok, 1 syntax errors)\\\\\\\\n64: //   u32     rule-name count R,     then R x (u32 len, UTF-8 bytes)\\\\\\\\n65: //   u32     symbolic-name count S, then S x (u32 len, UTF-8 bytes; \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" none)\\\\\\\\n66: //   u32     literal-name count S,  then S x (u32 len, UTF-8 bytes; \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" none)\\\\\\\\n67: //   u32     node count N, then N preorder records:\\\\\\\\n68: //             u8  kind (0 rule, 1 token)\\\\\\\\n69: //             rule:  u32 rule index, u32 child count,\\\\\\\\n70: //                    u8 has-start, i32 context start (start token's start)\\\\\\\\n71: //             token: i32 type, i32 start, i32 stop, i32 token index,\\\\\\\\n72: //                    u32 text len, UTF-8 text\\\\\\\\n73: //   u32     error count E, then E x\\\\\\\\n74: //             u32 line, u32 column, u32 len, UTF-8 message,\\\\\\\\n75: //             u8 span kind (0 none, 1 offending token, 2 lexer),\\\\\\\\n76: //             i32 a, i32 b (token start/stop, or lexer token-start char\\\\\\\\n77: //             index / input index when the error was reported),\\\\\\\\n78: //             i32 offending token type (-2 when there is no token)\\\\\\\\n79: //   first-failure evidence (the first error reported, lexer or parser):\\\\\\\\n80: //             u8 kind (0 none, 1 lexical, 2 token), u8 no-viable-alt,\\\\\\\\n81: //             i32 offending token index, u32 tokens buffered at the report\\\\\\\\n82: //   u32     buffered token count T after the parse, then T x\\\\\\\\n83: //             (i32 type, i32 token index, i32 start, i32 stop)\\\\\\\\n84: \\\\\\\\n85: #include <atomic>\\\\\\\\n86: #include <cstdint>\\\\\\\\n87: #include <cstdlib>\\\\\\\\n88: #include <cstring>\\\\\\\\n89: #include <limits>\\\\\\\\n90: #include <string>\\\\\\\\n91: #include <string_view>\\\\\\\\n92: #include <vector>\\\\\\\\n93: \\\\\\\\n94: #include \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"antlr4-runtime.h\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n95: #include \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"support/Utf8.h\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n96: #include \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Python3Lexer.h\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n97: #include \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Python3Parser.h\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n98: \\\\\\\\n99: // After the generated headers: Mach's headers define TRUE/FALSE, which are\\\\\\\\n100: // also generated token names.\\\\\\\\n101: #include <pthread.h>\\\\\\\\n102: #if defined(__APPLE__)\\\\\\\\n103: #include <malloc/malloc.h>\\\\\\\\n104: #elif defined(__GLIBC__)\\\\\\\\n105: #include <malloc.h>\\\\\\\\n106: #include <sys/syscall.h>\\\\\\\\n107: #include <unistd.h>\\\\\\\\n108: #endif\\\\\\\\n109: \\\\\\\\n110: #define JOLT_EXPORT extern \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"C\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" __attribute__((visibility(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"default\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")))\\\\\\\\n111: \\\\\\\\n112: namespace {\\\\\\\\n113: \\\\\\\\n114: constexpr size_t kMaxOutput = 64u * 1024u * 1024u;\\\\\\\\n115: \\\\\\\\n116: #ifdef JOLT_PARSER_TEST_SEAMS\\\\\\\\n117: // 0 off; 1 throw std::bad_alloc inside the parse; 2 throw a non-std\\\\\\\\n118: // exception; 3 as 1, and the failure handler's malloc fails too.\\\\\\\\n119: std::atomic<int32_t> g_fault{0};\\\\\\\\n120: \\\\\\\\n121: void maybe_fault() {\\\\\\\\n122:   switch (g_fault.load()) {\\\\\\\\n123:     case 1:\\\\\\\\n124:     case 3: throw std::bad_alloc();\\\\\\\\n125:     case 2: throw 42;\\\\\\\\n126:     default: break;\\\\\\\\n127:   }\\\\\\\\n128: }\\\\\\\\n129: \\\\\\\\n130: bool fail_handler_malloc() { return g_fault.load() == 3; }\\\\\\\\n131: #else\\\\\\\\n132: void maybe_fault() {}\\\\\\\\n133: bool fail_handler_malloc() { return false; }\\\\\\\\n134: #endif\\\\\\\\n135: \\\\\\\\n136: // Thrown (and caught by the entries) when the buffer would pass kMaxOutput.\\\\\\\\n137: struct Oversize {};\\\\\\\\n138: \\\\\\\\n139: struct Out {\\\\\\\\n140:   std::vector<uint8_t> buf;\\\\\\\\n141:   void room(size_t n) {\\\\\\\\n142:     if (n > kMaxOutput - buf.size()) throw Oversize{};\\\\\\\\n143:   }\\\\\\\\n144:   void u8(uint8_t v) {\\\\\\\\n145:     room(1);\\\\\\\\n146:     buf.push_back(v);\\\\\\\\n147:   }\\\\\\\\n148:   void u32(uint32_t v) {\\\\\\\\n149:     room(4);\\\\\\\\n150:     for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) buf.push_back(static_cast<uint8_t>(v >> (8 * i)));\\\\\\\\n151:   }\\\\\\\\n152:   void str(std::string_view s) {\\\\\\\\n153:     u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(s.size()));\\\\\\\\n154:     room(s.size());\\\\\\\\n155:     buf.insert(buf.end(), s.begin(), s.end());\\\\\\\\n156:   }\\\\\\\\n157: };\\\\\\\\n158: \\\\\\\\n159: uint32_t idx(size_t i) {\\\\\\\\n160:   return i > std::numeric_limits<uint32_t>::max()\\\\\\\\n161:              ? std::numeric_limits<uint32_t>::max()\\\\\\\\n162:              : static_cast<uint32_t>(i);\\\\\\\\n163: }\\\\\\\\n164: \\\\\\\\n165: struct Error {\\\\\\\\n166:   uint32_t line, column;\\\\\\\\n167:   std::string msg;\\\\\\\\n168: };\\\\\\\\n169: \\\\\\\\n170: class Collect : public antlr4::BaseErrorListener {\\\\\\\\n171:  public:\\\\\\\\n172:   std::vector<Error> errors;\\\\\\\\n173:   void syntaxError(antlr4::Recognizer*, antlr4::Token*, size_t line,\\\\\\\\n174:                    size_t column, const std::string& msg,\\\\\\\\n175:                    std::exception_ptr) override {\\\\\\\\n176:     errors.push_back({idx(line), idx(column), msg});\\\\\\\\n177:   }\\\\\\\\n178: };\\\\\\\\n179: \\\\\\\\n180: void walk(antlr4::tree::ParseTree* t, Out& out, uint32_t& count) {\\\\\\\\n181:   ++count;\\\\\\\\n182:   if (auto* term = dynamic_cast<antlr4::tree::TerminalNode*>(t)) {\\\\\\\\n183:     antlr4::Token* tok = term->getSymbol();\\\\\\\\n184:     out.u8(1);\\\\\\\\n185:     out.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(static_cast<int32_t>(tok->getType())));\\\\\\\\n186:     out.u32(idx(tok->getStartIndex()));\\\\\\\\n187:     out.u32(idx(tok->getStopIndex()));\\\\\\\\n188:     out.str(tok->getText());\\\\\\\\n189:     return;\\\\\\\\n190:   }\\\\\\\\n191:   auto* ctx = dynamic_cast<antlr4::ParserRuleContext*>(t);\\\\\\\\n192:   out.u8(0);\\\\\\\\n193:   out.u32(idx(ctx->getRuleIndex()));\\\\\\\\n194:   out.u32(idx(ctx->children.size()));\\\\\\\\n195:   for (auto* c : ctx->children) walk(c, out, count);\\\\\\\\n196: }\\\\\\\\n197: \\\\\\\\n198: int32_t hand_off(const std::vector<uint8_t>& bytes, uint8_t** out,\\\\\\\\n199:                  size_t* out_len) {\\\\\\\\n200:   if (bytes.size() > kMaxOutput) return -4;\\\\\\\\n201:   auto* p = static_cast<uint8_t*>(std::malloc(bytes.empty() ? 1 : bytes.size()));\\\\\\\\n202:   if (!p)