he migrated files |\\\\\\\\n733: |       |        |                                                                                | (§8.1).                                                           |\\\\\\\\n734: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\n735: | H3    | expand | `dao.host.hash`, `dao.host.sign`; `dao.jing` and `yin.vm.linker.sign` require  | Green; counts unchanged plus `dao.host.hash-test`; every corpus   |\\\\\\\\n736: |       | +migr. | them (`generate` stays, deferred). The string hash forms and `sign`'s `utf8`   | address identical; `sign_test` 4/4; `base64_test` 3/3 on three    |\\\\\\\\n737: |       |        | switch to `text/utf8-encode`: a **named behaviour change** for strings with an | lanes; a direct test that `digest-string` and `message` refuse an |\\\\\\\\n738: |       |        | unpaired surrogate (refusal instead of a substituted byte), recorded in the    | unpaired-surrogate string; **host-library gate (§8.2)**: within   |\\\\\\\\n739: |       |        | slice report; such strings are already refused by the canonical codec (corpus  | the adopted closure, no executable reference to `MessageDigest`,  |\\\\\\\\n740: |       |        | `unpaired-surrogate` class), so no persisted address changes. Base64 made      | `Blake3`, `noble`, `blake3_dart`, `package:crypto`,               |\\\\\\\\n741: |       |        | portable (table B; a replacement).                                             | `ed25519_edwards`, `goog.crypt.base64` outside `dao/host/`, and   |\\\\\\\\n742: |       |        |                                                                                | for the Ed25519 names outside `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`           |\\\\\\\\n743: |       |        |                                                                                | (`generate`); scan errors reported distinctly.                    |\\\\\\\\n744: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\n745: | H4    | migr.  | Portable Jing CBOR writer over `dao.host.*`; `dao.jing.cbor.boring` and        | Green; `cbor-v1.json` byte-identical on three lanes with the      |\\\\\\\\n746: |       |        | `dao.jing.cbor.cljd` deleted; Boring stays for `dao.stream.cbor.boring` and    | errata skips unchanged (`documented-skips-match-the-errata-and-   |\\\\\\\\n747: |       |        | the Dart `cbor` package for `dao.stream.cbor.cljd` (OQ4). A measurement:       | leave-no-case-unrun`); fixtures, DHT and linker image goldens     |\\\\\\\\n748: |       |        | corpus and one large module image, old writer against new, JVM and Node.       | unchanged; the measurement in the slice report, no threshold      |\\\\\\\\n749: |       |        |                                                                                | (OQ7). Slow tier once after landing.                              |\\\\\\\\n750: +-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\\\\\\\\n751: \\\\\\\\n752: Dependencies: H0, H1, H2 in order; H3 and H4 after H2, in either order.\\\\\\\\n753: \\\\\\\\n754: ### 8.1 List 1: the files permitted non-exempt host arms, baseline and final\\\\\\\\n755: \\\\\\\\n756: The gate never promises \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"no arms across `src/cljc`\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", only \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"no non-exempt\\\\\\\\n757: arms outside list 1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\". List 1 is generated at H0 by the gate from the actual\\\\\\\\n758: closure (every closure file holding a non-exempt arm, §3.3) and must equal\\\\\\\\n759: the **H0 baseline** below, by category, with each file's reason; a\\\\\\\\n760: difference either way is an H0 finding to resolve before H1. The baseline\\\\\\\\n761: is