{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"The artifacts confirm the main slow and Node timings, with two corrections: 976 seconds is the longest quick shard; the whole quick phase took 1,023 seconds. Also, `dao.space` and `yin.vm.ucf` took 109–110 seconds, so the “all other shards ≤37 seconds” claim is incorrect.\n\nThe full-coverage claim remains unproven. Node still has an unfinished residual shard and two terminated shards. Dart has only a completed six-namespace subset. Its current driver also drops the `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1` setting before launching Flutter, which could let a future green run skip slow bodies.\n"}}
